WEBVTT

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.230
Why do you want to ruin
what I have? Haven't you done enough?

00:00:34.864 --> 00:00:39.359
You do something like that again,
I'm calling the police. You understand me?

00:00:39.401 --> 00:00:41.574
Then you can
explain to Jeremiah and Hope

00:00:41.616 --> 00:00:44.001
why they have to pick you
up from the sheriff's office.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:50.930
This isn't about you, Sophie. This is
about them. They deserve to know.

00:00:51.004 --> 00:00:54.131
Why. What difference does it make?

00:00:55.007 --> 00:00:58.899
Based on your behavior today,
it could make a huge difference.

00:01:00.012 --> 00:01:01.971
You're the problem, not me.

00:01:02.013 --> 00:01:04.122
You know, the way you treated me was bad

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:06.691
enough, but now you
want to ruin what I have?

00:01:07.628 --> 00:01:10.838
No wonder your own daughter
doesn't talk to you anymore.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.115
You have till the weekend.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:29.328
You tell them or we will.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.234
They have a right to
know. And that's all I have to say.

00:01:34.718 --> 00:01:37.613
We're done here.

00:01:37.655 --> 00:01:39.584
Now, please...

00:01:40.365 --> 00:01:41.460
Leave.

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:50.573
Sophie.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:19.440
Look, we're not going to
make you go if you really don't want to...

00:02:19.665 --> 00:02:23.181
But it wouldn't
hurt to talk to someone.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.177
I'm talking to you.

00:02:26.219 --> 00:02:27.922
I'm not a psychiatrist.

00:02:29.171 --> 00:02:30.821
Psychologist.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.799
Psychiatrists prescribe meds.

00:02:35.346 --> 00:02:37.823
Yeah, I'll prescribe you
something if you correct me again.

00:02:39.073 --> 00:02:43.256
I don't want to go to a
doctor. You're my dad.

00:02:43.298 --> 00:02:45.597
You were a cop. You
know what it's like to...

00:02:46.924 --> 00:02:51.140
do what I did. Why would
I talk to someone else?

00:02:56.998 --> 00:02:59.214
I know it's Hope.

00:02:59.401 --> 00:03:01.671
Mom. Pushing this.

00:03:01.713 --> 00:03:03.671
What's her deal?

00:03:03.713 --> 00:03:07.415
She doesn't have a 'deal', Sophie,
she's just worried about you.

00:03:08.118 --> 00:03:10.664
I'm fine. I've been fine.

00:03:11.992 --> 00:03:15.621
That's kind of what she's concerned about.

00:03:17.577 --> 00:03:19.709
Do you agree with her?

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.145
No.

00:03:22.574 --> 00:03:25.096
Not necessarily, but I - I
understand why she's worried.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.994
When you were a cop,
you had to kill before.

00:03:33.385 --> 00:03:35.922
Twice. Right?

00:03:35.964 --> 00:03:39.720
And then, there was the
guy who broke in here.

00:03:39.762 --> 00:03:41.762
Yeah, screw that guy.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.678
Did you need counseling?

00:03:47.421 --> 00:03:49.528
No.

00:03:49.570 --> 00:03:55.162
Uh, I did have a 'Fitness for Duty'
evaluation after the second one, but no.

00:03:56.474 --> 00:03:58.282
What was different about the second one?

00:03:59.375 --> 00:04:02.883
Uh, it was a pretty
clear suicide by cop case.

00:04:04.283 --> 00:04:06.542
I didn't want to have to shoot him, but...

00:04:09.131 --> 00:04:11.525
You did what you had to do.

00:04:13.435 --> 00:04:15.003
Yeah.

00:04:15.045 --> 00:04:18.954
Someone tried to murder
my mom right in front of me.

00:04:20.828 --> 00:04:22.633
I did what I had to do. I -

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:27.679
I don't feel bad about it. I don't
regret it. I - I would do it again.

00:04:28.013 --> 00:04:30.000
I would do anything to protect you guys.

00:04:30.508 --> 00:04:32.968
And I don't see why anyone
would think that's a problem.

00:04:33.355 --> 00:04:34.871
Hey, listen.

00:04:36.119 --> 00:04:37.845
No one thinks it's a problem.

00:04:38.357 --> 00:04:41.584
Hope is only trying to
make sure you're okay.

00:04:42.331 --> 00:04:45.469
Not everyone's as strong
as you apparently are.

00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.010
But... any parent.

00:04:49.144 --> 00:04:52.862
Anyone who really cares -
they would do the same thing.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.684
Okay.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:20.090
John.

00:05:26.571 --> 00:05:28.287
John.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.600
Something's wrong.

00:05:52.973 --> 00:05:54.739
John!

00:05:56.421 --> 00:05:58.962
G - get help!

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.696
Okay.

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:49.440
Sophie?

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:16.692
Hey, what are you doing up?

00:09:17.123 --> 00:09:19.123
I've been having trouble sleeping.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:21.389
You?

00:09:21.754 --> 00:09:23.754
Uh. I was thirsty.

00:09:24.328 --> 00:09:25.313
M-hm.

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:28.217
And so you went
to the store to get a water

00:09:28.259 --> 00:09:30.080
bottle instead of drinking
what we have here?

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:34.640
Or was that another skinny teenager I
saw out the window a couple of minutes ago?

00:09:41.123 --> 00:09:43.982
Get some sleep. We'll talk tomorrow.

00:09:44.372 --> 00:09:47.772
Jeremiah will wake up if I'm out of bed too
long and then you'd really be in trouble.

00:09:48.849 --> 00:09:50.484
I'm sorry.

00:09:50.598 --> 00:09:51.931
Yeah.

00:09:51.973 --> 00:09:53.426
And you're grounded.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:57.983
Good night.

00:09:58.445 --> 00:10:00.000
Night.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:11.530
Sophie.

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:16.570
Are you okay?

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:23.526
If you need something, if - if
you need someone to talk to...

00:10:27.040 --> 00:10:28.404
I'm fine.

00:10:29.351 --> 00:10:31.351
Thanks. Night.

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:47.779
Oh, come on.
I'll just be a minute.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:54.485
Hey, you're up. Mhm.

00:11:00.968 --> 00:11:02.724
Who's at the door?

00:11:04.208 --> 00:11:05.374
Just...

00:11:12.647 --> 00:11:14.647
The hell...

00:11:23.933 --> 00:11:25.126
Really?

00:11:25.396 --> 00:11:28.567
I'm not trying to get
sick. I have practice today.

00:11:29.065 --> 00:11:31.023
You probably already have it.

00:11:31.065 --> 00:11:34.619
Be careful doing
all those kicks and flips.

00:11:35.121 --> 00:11:38.527
How embarrassing would it
be to puke all over your friends?

00:11:38.588 --> 00:11:40.041
Sophie.

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:44.880
I'll say grace.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:48.495
Thank you, Lord, for this food.

00:11:48.537 --> 00:11:51.236
And please bless the meal
and the hands that prepared it.

00:11:52.737 --> 00:11:54.549
Wait, who cooked this morning?

00:11:55.107 --> 00:11:56.201
I did.

00:11:57.217 --> 00:11:59.578
And please keep Daddy
and me from getting sick.

00:11:59.747 --> 00:12:01.740
'Daddy and I' you twit.

00:12:02.914 --> 00:12:03.878
Ow.

00:12:03.920 --> 00:12:05.903
In Jesus's name. Amen.

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:12.659
So, you think you guys caught
a bug or just something you ate?

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:17.822
I don't think you
had anything we didn't have.

00:12:18.134 --> 00:12:20.731
Unless you got a snack or something
when you were up last night.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:25.799
Just water.

00:12:26.971 --> 00:12:29.459
I have a headache, but I
don't really think that I'm sick.

00:12:30.153 --> 00:12:32.387
I don't have a headache, just...

00:12:33.012 --> 00:12:35.082
I don't know. Nauseous?

00:12:35.472 --> 00:12:39.517
All right. How about we talk about
something else before we all get sick?

00:12:39.954 --> 00:12:41.485
Good idea.

00:12:41.932 --> 00:12:43.932
Yeah.

00:13:02.251 --> 00:13:04.040
Um.

00:13:04.082 --> 00:13:08.347
I have more work to do, but I think
I'm going to go lay down for a little.

00:13:09.627 --> 00:13:11.440
Is your headache getting worse?

00:13:12.084 --> 00:13:14.678
Yeah, I'm afraid so. Um.

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:18.417
Can you just come get me if I'm
not awake after like an hour, please?

00:13:18.735 --> 00:13:20.735
Yeah, sure.

00:13:25.368 --> 00:13:26.627
Sophie.

00:13:28.891 --> 00:13:30.791
You're a good kid.

00:13:31.065 --> 00:13:36.033
And I know that you respect us
despite what happened last night.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:41.457
I'm trusting that you weren't out
doing anything we need to discuss.

00:13:41.596 --> 00:13:43.596
No.

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:46.617
It was stupid.

00:13:47.051 --> 00:13:49.754
And I - I was
alone and no drugs. Never.

00:13:51.928 --> 00:13:53.373
Okay.

00:13:54.306 --> 00:13:56.668
And I don't have
to tell you how dumb it

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:59.063
is for you to be out at
that hour by yourself?

00:13:59.688 --> 00:14:01.190
Jeremiah has my location.

00:14:01.232 --> 00:14:03.469
That's besides the point, Sophie.

00:14:05.367 --> 00:14:08.538
I know. I won't do it again. I'm sorry.

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:12.484
Okay.

00:14:12.904 --> 00:14:14.904
I hope you feel better.

00:14:15.763 --> 00:14:17.556
Are you doing okay?

00:14:17.598 --> 00:14:19.166
Yeah, actually.

00:14:19.208 --> 00:14:21.208
Feel fine, now.

00:14:21.427 --> 00:14:23.427
Good. Seeya.

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.606
Sophie.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:51.299
Their employees called
in a welfare check this morning-

00:14:51.341 --> 00:14:54.948
- when they didn't show up.
And they weren't answering their phones.

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:57.795
So Hoyte went
and their cars were in

00:14:57.837 --> 00:15:00.621
the driveway, but no
one answered the door.

00:15:01.871 --> 00:15:03.796
He forced entry and...

00:15:04.509 --> 00:15:06.197
How did they die?

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:09.810
It's... it's ironic.

00:15:10.793 --> 00:15:13.340
Gas leak.

00:15:14.105 --> 00:15:17.190
The pigtail hose
behind their stove was fairly old.

00:15:17.232 --> 00:15:20.560
And it looks like a rodent
chewed through it over time or something.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:27.067
We don't know how long it's been
like that, but the levels were really high.

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:30.886
Hoyte said he smelled something
the second he opened the door.

00:15:31.669 --> 00:15:33.357
Their detectors?

00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:35.844
Dead batteries.

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:40.832
I know it stinks, but there's
no evidence of foul play and...

00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:46.383
I don't know. Sometimes I think everything
just comes together for the worst outcome.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:55.269
Sophie, you up?

00:17:03.680 --> 00:17:04.570
No.

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:24.093
Sophie.

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:29.457
You scared the hell out of me.

00:17:29.687 --> 00:17:30.906
I'm sorry.

00:17:32.084 --> 00:17:34.084
What time is it?

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:38.394
Oh, shoot. Oh...

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:45.945
You taking this hard?

00:17:46.301 --> 00:17:50.644
No. No. I have a headache or
a migraine or something. But...

00:17:52.895 --> 00:17:55.139
I'm sorry for your loss, Brooke.

00:17:56.297 --> 00:18:00.000
They were your parents, too.
You know. For a while, at least.

00:18:00.918 --> 00:18:03.425
Oh, not really. I mean...

00:18:04.263 --> 00:18:06.263
Gave me a place to stay.

00:18:06.801 --> 00:18:08.801
Took care of me. Fed me.

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:11.655
Which I'm thankful for. But...

00:18:12.340 --> 00:18:15.000
Yeah, but... what else do parents do?

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:24.928
Um, I still follow you on Instagram
even though you don't really post anymore.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:28.518
I saw that you got adopted by
that family you used to babysit for.

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:30.000
And you seem really happy.

00:18:30.528 --> 00:18:32.528
I am. Very.

00:18:33.419 --> 00:18:35.419
Speaking of which, I have to get home.

00:18:38.094 --> 00:18:39.425
Um.

00:18:40.346 --> 00:18:44.298
Are - are you going to be alone
here? How long are you in town?

00:18:44.633 --> 00:18:48.231
Um... I just came to see them.

00:18:48.273 --> 00:18:50.709
But um, Uncle Dave and
Aunt Julie will be here in

00:18:50.751 --> 00:18:52.839
a couple hours, so I'll
probably head out then.

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:55.646
Can't really stay until
the end of the semester.

00:18:55.688 --> 00:18:58.348
But they left me the house, so...

00:18:58.390 --> 00:19:00.390
Gotta clean up that mess.

00:19:01.779 --> 00:19:03.301
What about the funeral?

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:08.095
They wanted to be cremated,
so there's no rush on that, I guess.

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:13.973
Um, I'm sorry I stopped
responding on Instagram.

00:19:16.045 --> 00:19:18.416
There was so
much going on and I wasn't

00:19:18.458 --> 00:19:20.822
on good speaking terms
with your parents and...

00:19:20.864 --> 00:19:23.006
I didn't mean to take it out on you.

00:19:23.048 --> 00:19:25.527
No, it's fine. Don't
worry about it. I - I could

00:19:25.569 --> 00:19:28.090
have done more to stay
in touch, too. It's cool.

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:31.535
Can we uh...

00:19:31.753 --> 00:19:33.441
Start over?

00:19:34.207 --> 00:19:38.159
How about we just pick up where we
left off and then not leave off again?

00:19:41.023 --> 00:19:42.711
Yeah.

00:19:51.371 --> 00:19:52.725
You okay?

00:19:53.714 --> 00:19:54.933
Yeah.

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:11.566
Thank you.

00:20:16.251 --> 00:20:17.692
How you doing?

00:20:19.181 --> 00:20:21.181
My head might be a little better.

00:20:21.943 --> 00:20:23.943
Good.

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:31.413
We got two chapters left?
What are we reading next?

00:20:31.455 --> 00:20:33.977
Uh, I was thinking Job.

00:20:34.393 --> 00:20:36.649
Should do something
in the Old Testament and

00:20:36.691 --> 00:20:39.439
I haven't read it in... years.

00:20:40.663 --> 00:20:42.663
Cool.

00:20:49.084 --> 00:20:51.227
Is it weird that...

00:20:52.207 --> 00:20:54.604
Okay, I'm sorry they're gone.

00:20:55.120 --> 00:21:00.000
But I don't know how I feel
about it. I'm not exactly sad.

00:21:01.226 --> 00:21:03.184
Grief's always different.

00:21:03.226 --> 00:21:07.566
I think especially when the people
who died weren't all that great.

00:21:09.218 --> 00:21:13.103
Honestly, I still have to
pray about being angry, sometimes.

00:21:13.235 --> 00:21:15.235
It's not right, but...

00:21:16.406 --> 00:21:19.259
When I think about how they treated you...

00:21:19.649 --> 00:21:21.180
It's hard.

00:21:24.091 --> 00:21:30.000
But they could have made the adoption
process a lot more complicated, so...

00:21:31.517 --> 00:21:33.278
I do owe them for that.

00:21:34.534 --> 00:21:36.534
Yeah, me too.

00:21:42.337 --> 00:21:44.607
That being said.

00:21:44.860 --> 00:21:47.037
If you see them when you die...

00:21:48.287 --> 00:21:49.593
you didn't go to heaven.

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:53.217
That is an awful thing
to say.

00:21:57.200 --> 00:22:00.703
Oh, no. I - I was doing fine this morning.

00:22:08.480 --> 00:22:10.474
Jeremiah Tatum? Hm?

00:22:10.559 --> 00:22:12.517
You want to explain this to me?

00:22:12.559 --> 00:22:14.581
What? I ain't do nothin'.

00:22:16.825 --> 00:22:18.200
You definitely did something.

00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:27.520
What the hell is that?

00:22:28.117 --> 00:22:31.054
Um, it's the third one.

00:22:36.970 --> 00:22:39.198
Who'd you get to pee on it?

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:41.474
Was it Kayla? Shut up.

00:22:47.680 --> 00:22:49.101
What's going on?

00:22:50.212 --> 00:22:52.170
You're um...

00:22:52.212 --> 00:22:54.430
You're going to be a big sister this time.

00:22:57.770 --> 00:22:58.949
Wait.

00:23:01.370 --> 00:23:04.945
What? Are you kidding? Are you kidding?

00:23:10.490 --> 00:23:12.219
Is that why you've been sick?

00:23:12.430 --> 00:23:14.430
Yeah.

00:23:17.920 --> 00:23:20.802
Sophie. Oh, don't you dare.

00:23:37.280 --> 00:23:39.926
Hey, I'm really
sorry I didn't answer your text.

00:23:40.297 --> 00:23:44.958
It's okay. I probably should've
gotten over myself and just gone today.

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:48.143
At least for you.
We sent flowers. I just...

00:23:48.185 --> 00:23:51.085
The flowers were so nice.
Thank you so much and um...

00:23:51.127 --> 00:23:53.127
Please thank your parents for me, but...

00:23:54.015 --> 00:23:57.044
I'm actually glad you
didn't go. It was a mess.

00:23:57.157 --> 00:23:58.532
What do you mean?

00:23:58.625 --> 00:24:03.640
Well, my parents were really well off
so there's a lot to sort through, and...

00:24:03.682 --> 00:24:05.981
I thought we could do it
in the next couple days.

00:24:06.023 --> 00:24:08.130
Even tomorrow would
have been better, but...

00:24:08.520 --> 00:24:12.369
No, the coffins were
barely in the ground and...

00:24:12.411 --> 00:24:16.071
Aunt Julie and Uncle Dave were already
talking about the will and the assets.

00:24:16.125 --> 00:24:18.125
That's...

00:24:18.672 --> 00:24:20.672
I'm sorry.

00:24:21.537 --> 00:24:25.474
I think they wanted the house, I
guess, but my parents left that to me.

00:24:25.844 --> 00:24:28.895
And... a lot of their money. Um...

00:24:28.937 --> 00:24:32.404
Anyway, uh, they brought
out some papers for me to sign.

00:24:32.446 --> 00:24:35.250
And when I said I had to
think about it they started

00:24:35.292 --> 00:24:37.870
screaming and saying
they would contest it all.

00:24:37.912 --> 00:24:41.907
And they want to go to
court, or something. I don't...

00:24:41.949 --> 00:24:45.421
I just wanted to bury my parents. I
still have three more weeks of school.

00:24:45.463 --> 00:24:48.092
I just, I - I don't want to
deal with this right now.

00:24:49.467 --> 00:24:51.779
I'm assuming
you're skipping the repass?

00:24:55.120 --> 00:24:57.379
Hey, you want
to come here for lunch?

00:24:58.381 --> 00:25:00.964
I - I don't want to be a drag. Um.

00:25:01.006 --> 00:25:06.320
I'll probably just stay here and
eat ice cream and cry into my pillow.

00:25:07.040 --> 00:25:09.039
You can eat ice cream here.

00:25:09.081 --> 00:25:12.040
And just bring your
pillow. My mom said you're welcome.

00:25:16.570 --> 00:25:20.935
Thank you so much, Hope. Um, I've gotten
so used to eating ramen and fast food.

00:25:20.977 --> 00:25:24.147
I literally don't remember the
last time I had a home-cooked meal.

00:25:24.636 --> 00:25:26.594
I hope it didn't disappoint.

00:25:26.636 --> 00:25:28.154
Oh, absolutely not.

00:25:28.385 --> 00:25:31.244
Good. You're welcome, anytime.

00:25:32.522 --> 00:25:34.522
When are you going back to school?

00:25:35.200 --> 00:25:39.114
Um, I have to talk to my parents'
lawyer and get all the paperwork done...

00:25:39.156 --> 00:25:41.941
In the next -
like, hopefully - 3, 4 days.

00:25:41.983 --> 00:25:43.983
Um, and then I'll head back, I guess.

00:25:44.982 --> 00:25:46.513
Doesn't school start Monday?

00:25:46.681 --> 00:25:49.228
Yeah, but - ugh, like - what else can I do?

00:25:50.573 --> 00:25:53.101
Well, I'm pretty sure we
can get you back in 2 days.

00:25:53.143 --> 00:25:55.143
If you're willing
to put in the work.

00:25:55.486 --> 00:25:56.821
What do you mean?

00:25:57.694 --> 00:26:00.433
I mean, there's going to
be a ton of paperwork to file.

00:26:00.475 --> 00:26:04.783
Um, some affidavits, but you
can do most of that online really.

00:26:04.825 --> 00:26:06.414
There's
transferring bills depending

00:26:06.418 --> 00:26:08.086
on what you want to
do with the house and...

00:26:08.090 --> 00:26:10.090
Just getting
ready for probate court.

00:26:11.120 --> 00:26:13.911
It's a process, but I can help.

00:26:14.113 --> 00:26:17.441
And even walk you through
some steps when you get back to school.

00:26:17.815 --> 00:26:21.352
You're still going to need a lawyer, but
I can assist with some of the leg work.

00:26:24.320 --> 00:26:28.151
Cool. So, I understood like
maybe 30% of what you just said.

00:26:28.193 --> 00:26:30.884
So if you'd be willing
to help I'd be so grateful.

00:26:30.926 --> 00:26:33.383
All right. We need to
get to your house and

00:26:33.425 --> 00:26:35.981
go through what's
there. First things first.

00:26:36.371 --> 00:26:38.728
Okay, yeah. Sure, sure. Um... when?

00:26:39.297 --> 00:26:40.516
Um...

00:26:40.979 --> 00:26:45.340
You girls handle the dishes. I'm going to
go pull some things up and call our lawyer.

00:26:45.382 --> 00:26:46.913
We leave in ten.

00:26:48.588 --> 00:26:50.588
Oh, my gosh.

00:27:00.480 --> 00:27:02.688
Wow. I know it's so cool.

00:27:07.920 --> 00:27:08.987
Something wrong?

00:27:16.483 --> 00:27:18.030
That gas hurt?

00:27:18.150 --> 00:27:20.150
You're so stupid.

00:27:26.891 --> 00:27:28.652
Really? Today?

00:27:29.254 --> 00:27:30.615
I know.

00:27:30.657 --> 00:27:33.377
It's the new guy, he
probably forgot a code or something.

00:27:33.531 --> 00:27:35.062
Just a minute.

00:27:41.747 --> 00:27:43.465
Where are you girls going?

00:27:57.771 --> 00:28:00.459
Girls, slow down.

00:28:21.611 --> 00:28:24.653
Girls, we should wait for Jeremiah.

00:28:28.480 --> 00:28:30.534
We're going
to play hide and seek.

00:28:30.576 --> 00:28:32.339
Yeah, no peeking.

00:29:08.560 --> 00:29:10.973
Candace.

00:29:11.015 --> 00:29:12.682
Sophie.

00:29:15.000 --> 00:29:19.010
One. Two.

00:29:20.883 --> 00:29:22.883
Three.

00:29:27.600 --> 00:29:30.000
Four. Five.

00:29:30.698 --> 00:29:32.698
Six.

00:29:32.808 --> 00:29:34.804
Seven.

00:29:34.846 --> 00:29:36.846
Eight.

00:29:37.034 --> 00:29:38.565
Nine.

00:29:38.914 --> 00:29:40.211
Ten.

00:30:23.920 --> 00:30:25.526
What's wrong?

00:30:26.485 --> 00:30:28.485
You okay?

00:30:31.200 --> 00:30:32.661
Yeah.

00:30:33.818 --> 00:30:35.818
Just a bad dream.

00:30:36.025 --> 00:30:38.025
Freaked me out.

00:30:39.142 --> 00:30:41.142
Again?

00:30:43.360 --> 00:30:45.000
It's okay. I'm fine.

00:30:47.520 --> 00:30:51.314
Go back to sleep. I'll be right back.

00:30:51.643 --> 00:30:53.643
Alright.

00:31:07.982 --> 00:31:09.581
Sophie.

00:31:10.440 --> 00:31:13.970
You nearly gave me a
heart attack. What are you doing up?

00:31:22.013 --> 00:31:23.853
Sophie?

00:31:44.170 --> 00:31:45.638
Sophie.

00:32:58.010 --> 00:33:02.617
I haven't opened it all yet, but
so far it's all confirmations and notices.

00:33:02.806 --> 00:33:06.324
Well, I am struggling with work, but um...

00:33:06.366 --> 00:33:08.950
If you want to come
over for dinner later...

00:33:08.992 --> 00:33:11.444
Or just to hang out in the
meantime, you're more than welcome.

00:33:11.486 --> 00:33:13.303
And then we can go over everything.

00:33:13.405 --> 00:33:16.598
Um... can I come
tomorrow? For dinner?

00:33:16.640 --> 00:33:19.288
Um, I have to
be here until 3 or 4. The

00:33:19.330 --> 00:33:21.908
insurance company is
sending an investigator.

00:33:21.950 --> 00:33:25.190
M-hm. Yeah, that's
typical with these claims.

00:33:25.312 --> 00:33:28.038
It's nothing to worry about.
It's actually a good sign.

00:33:28.080 --> 00:33:30.000
Means things are moving along.

00:33:30.172 --> 00:33:32.172
If you say so.

00:33:32.697 --> 00:33:34.655
You sure you don't need anything today?

00:33:34.697 --> 00:33:38.008
No, no, I'm all good.
I'm just, uh, getting settled in.

00:33:38.339 --> 00:33:40.339
Alright, well...

00:33:40.741 --> 00:33:43.360
We're here if you change your
mind. Thanks, Hope.

00:33:43.565 --> 00:33:45.955
Yeah, um.
Please tell Sophie I said 'hi'.

00:33:46.460 --> 00:33:48.772
Will do. See you tomorrow.

00:33:52.810 --> 00:33:56.282
Why is the insurance company
sending an investigator?

00:33:56.359 --> 00:33:58.477
It's just to make sure
there's no suspicious

00:33:58.519 --> 00:34:00.343
circumstances surrounding the deaths.

00:34:01.201 --> 00:34:02.847
Wasn't it an accident?

00:34:03.160 --> 00:34:04.705
Yeah, well...

00:34:04.747 --> 00:34:06.507
With large life insurance claims, it's

00:34:06.549 --> 00:34:08.778
typical to have an
independent investigation.

00:34:10.273 --> 00:34:11.726
Hm.

00:34:15.680 --> 00:34:19.017
Hey, when you get a chance, can
you review this? I want to take a walk.

00:34:19.544 --> 00:34:23.583
Uh, yeah. You can
go now. I'll check it later.

00:34:23.625 --> 00:34:25.759
I um...

00:34:25.801 --> 00:34:28.582
I'm super slow in my work
right now. I need to catch up.

00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:32.020
Maybe after a nap.

00:34:32.588 --> 00:34:34.041
Pregnancy brain.

00:34:35.583 --> 00:34:37.583
Speaking of 'walking'...

00:34:39.517 --> 00:34:42.244
Were you sleepwalking last night?

00:34:42.286 --> 00:34:45.000
Or do you remember
giving me a heart attack?

00:34:47.440 --> 00:34:49.154
I don't sleepwalk.

00:34:49.214 --> 00:34:51.214
And I didn't get up.

00:34:53.840 --> 00:34:56.733
Haven't you been having nightmares?

00:34:57.918 --> 00:35:00.387
No I... I wasn't dreaming.

00:35:03.840 --> 00:35:05.120
If you say so.

00:35:20.960 --> 00:35:22.353
Mom.

00:35:22.665 --> 00:35:24.665
Mom-

00:36:43.930 --> 00:36:45.720
Is there someone at the door?

00:36:53.608 --> 00:36:56.093
Is there anyone at the door?

00:37:09.120 --> 00:37:10.360
Hey.

00:37:11.110 --> 00:37:13.068
What are you on about?

00:37:14.641 --> 00:37:15.860
What's that noise?

00:37:18.560 --> 00:37:20.274
All I hear is the oven.

00:37:20.326 --> 00:37:22.014
Be quiet and listen.

00:37:26.320 --> 00:37:29.491
Of course now it's gone.
You - you didn't hear anything?

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:31.594
No.

00:37:31.636 --> 00:37:35.891
15 minutes? Come on, Sophie. You
have to have dinner ready by seven.

00:37:35.933 --> 00:37:37.606
At the latest.

00:37:37.686 --> 00:37:38.827
Hm?

00:37:41.680 --> 00:37:42.733
How did?

00:37:52.417 --> 00:37:54.145
Wh-what?

00:37:55.785 --> 00:37:58.745
Candace, why are you
quarantining your Brussels sprouts?

00:37:58.817 --> 00:38:01.442
-You have to eat them.
-But they're gross.

00:38:12.317 --> 00:38:16.660
A ten billion dollar aircraft?

00:38:19.521 --> 00:38:21.921
It's not New York
City so I'll take the aircraft.

00:38:22.337 --> 00:38:24.685
Why do you not want
to live in New York City?

00:38:24.727 --> 00:38:26.812
There's many
reasons for that - wait. Aircraft?

00:38:26.816 --> 00:38:29.285
What? Who would pick the
apartment?

00:38:29.688 --> 00:38:32.074
Even if you like New York, right?

00:38:33.248 --> 00:38:36.264
Well, the aircraft is in the air.

00:38:36.837 --> 00:38:37.978
Okay.

00:39:19.120 --> 00:39:20.183
Sophie.

00:44:18.640 --> 00:44:19.737
Hey, Brooke. What's up?

00:44:21.321 --> 00:44:23.321
The insurance company called back.

00:44:23.642 --> 00:44:27.493
It - it wasn't what they thought.
Somebody did this to my parents.

00:44:27.535 --> 00:44:29.535
Brooke, slow down. What are you saying?

00:44:31.200 --> 00:44:33.798
The corrosion didn't
cause a leak. Apparently...

00:44:33.840 --> 00:44:37.977
There were distinct cuts made by a
tool probably the day that my parents died.

00:44:43.600 --> 00:44:45.000
Sophie?

00:44:48.560 --> 00:44:50.105
Sophie, are you okay?

00:44:54.165 --> 00:44:55.387
Sophie.

00:45:15.691 --> 00:45:17.128
Sophie.

00:45:19.174 --> 00:45:21.174
Sophie.

00:45:23.292 --> 00:45:24.735
You okay?

00:45:26.358 --> 00:45:28.983
No. I'm scared.

00:45:29.875 --> 00:45:31.016
What are you scared of?

00:45:32.307 --> 00:45:34.307
There's something wrong with me.

00:45:34.810 --> 00:45:36.728
There's nothing wrong with you.

00:45:36.886 --> 00:45:39.745
I think you passed out.
You must've had a... panic attack.

00:45:39.999 --> 00:45:41.140
That's it.

00:45:46.880 --> 00:45:48.538
Sophie, breathe.

00:45:48.919 --> 00:45:52.403
Breathe. In and
out through your nostrils. Okay?

00:45:52.647 --> 00:45:53.902
Come on.

00:46:20.088 --> 00:46:21.212
They were murdered?

00:46:21.962 --> 00:46:23.572
Looks that way.

00:46:24.333 --> 00:46:26.333
Kayla's coming over
to tell us more about it.

00:46:27.778 --> 00:46:30.403
Brooke. I - I was on the
phone with her. Is she okay?

00:46:31.051 --> 00:46:32.440
She's fine.

00:46:33.377 --> 00:46:35.368
She called us when you stopped answering.

00:46:36.510 --> 00:46:38.550
She's still coming over
for dinner in a little bit.

00:46:41.920 --> 00:46:46.535
Sophie, I know your relationship
with them was complicated, but...

00:46:47.785 --> 00:46:49.875
Whatever you're
feeling right now is normal.

00:46:50.725 --> 00:46:54.518
It's one thing if it was an
accident. But if they were murdered...

00:46:54.560 --> 00:46:58.457
It's not all about them.

00:46:59.521 --> 00:47:01.521
What else is there?

00:47:02.656 --> 00:47:04.656
I should've told you guys
as soon as I found out.

00:47:07.360 --> 00:47:09.080
They wouldn't tell me how they knew, but...

00:47:09.835 --> 00:47:12.929
My birth mom. Sheila. She-

00:47:13.469 --> 00:47:15.469
She's in a psych hospital.

00:47:16.890 --> 00:47:21.196
She had a violent episode and she was
she was diagnosed with schizophrenia.

00:47:22.672 --> 00:47:25.023
The last time I saw John and Melissa...

00:47:25.570 --> 00:47:27.514
They were going to tell you if I didn't.

00:47:28.251 --> 00:47:30.485
Well, why would that
matter? You didn't do anything.

00:47:33.840 --> 00:47:35.526
It's genetic.

00:47:38.160 --> 00:47:41.701
The headaches,
sleepwalking, the passing out.

00:47:41.743 --> 00:47:43.701
You don't have schizophrenia, Sophie.

00:47:43.743 --> 00:47:45.069
You don't know that.

00:47:45.648 --> 00:47:47.135
Something's wrong with me.

00:47:48.133 --> 00:47:49.274
Sophie.

00:47:50.509 --> 00:47:52.509
That's not true.

00:47:52.613 --> 00:47:54.925
They showed me pictures
of the doctor she attacked.

00:47:56.741 --> 00:47:58.627
I can't get them out of my head.

00:48:00.459 --> 00:48:01.756
His eyes.

00:48:02.410 --> 00:48:04.800
She gouged his eyes out.

00:48:05.603 --> 00:48:07.561
What if-

00:48:07.603 --> 00:48:11.133
What if I - You don't have
schi - schizophrenia, Sophie.

00:48:11.820 --> 00:48:15.000
Just because it's genetic, that
doesn't mean you're going to get it.

00:48:18.240 --> 00:48:19.979
What if I do?

00:48:56.810 --> 00:48:58.836
I bought you some stuff.

00:48:59.739 --> 00:49:01.739
Kayla, I told you not to.

00:49:02.194 --> 00:49:05.903
I got you a weighted sleep mask
since you've been getting up at night.

00:49:06.403 --> 00:49:07.814
And a bath set.

00:49:07.856 --> 00:49:09.270
Scented candles...

00:49:09.442 --> 00:49:12.379
Some salts and... cream
Jeremiah can put on for you, later.

00:49:15.440 --> 00:49:19.591
I know you haven't been doing great
lately. You got to take care of yourself.

00:49:22.011 --> 00:49:23.261
Thank you.

00:49:25.135 --> 00:49:26.619
In the meantime...

00:49:27.413 --> 00:49:30.872
We are reopening the investigation
into John's and Melissa's deaths.

00:49:30.914 --> 00:49:33.711
We think it was, uh...
asphyxiation by homicide.

00:49:38.240 --> 00:49:40.450
There were tool marks on the tubing.

00:49:40.550 --> 00:49:43.409
And there was no
oxidation or dust in the kerf.

00:49:44.255 --> 00:49:45.718
Uh...

00:49:45.760 --> 00:49:49.267
A lot of damage was fresh
and consistent with tool usage.

00:49:50.883 --> 00:49:52.883
Someone made the leak happen.

00:49:58.080 --> 00:50:01.463
Um, are - are there any
suspects yet? Off the record.

00:50:01.588 --> 00:50:04.213
It's so early, we have no idea.

00:50:05.133 --> 00:50:07.733
But someone will need
to speak to Sophie soon.

00:50:08.747 --> 00:50:10.747
Uh - as a suspect?

00:50:10.862 --> 00:50:12.862
No, as someone who lived with them.

00:50:13.200 --> 00:50:17.257
She might know if they had any
enemies or anyone with incentive.

00:50:19.210 --> 00:50:20.526
Right.

00:50:29.360 --> 00:50:30.330
Hey.

00:50:31.768 --> 00:50:33.143
I'm so sorry.

00:50:38.799 --> 00:50:40.799
Come here.

00:50:47.120 --> 00:50:48.635
So, who do you think did it?

00:50:48.677 --> 00:50:51.380
-Candace.
-No, it's okay. Um.

00:50:51.700 --> 00:50:55.470
I don't know. I mean my parents
weren't exactly popular with everyone.

00:50:55.939 --> 00:50:59.229
Except for their employees.
Apparently, they were very good bosses.

00:51:00.400 --> 00:51:02.057
Well, Daddy couldn't stand them.

00:51:03.259 --> 00:51:05.259
But, I know
he was home that night.

00:51:05.876 --> 00:51:07.678
And he is a good Christian.

00:51:07.720 --> 00:51:10.345
Even though he has
shot a few people before.

00:51:10.882 --> 00:51:12.541
About to shoot one more tonight.

00:51:14.053 --> 00:51:17.013
I don't know. I'm just hoping
that the insurance guy got it wrong.

00:51:17.031 --> 00:51:20.124
Or... maybe he just
didn't want to pay out the money.

00:51:20.800 --> 00:51:23.024
Well, that would be
best case scenario, but...

00:51:23.066 --> 00:51:27.318
Well, Kayla already double
checked so that ain't it.

00:51:27.360 --> 00:51:28.798
Can we talk about something else?

00:51:29.086 --> 00:51:30.762
I'm trying to help Brooke.

00:51:30.804 --> 00:51:34.246
If they did it for the
money then you'll be next in line.

00:51:34.288 --> 00:51:37.699
So maybe you shouldn't stay
in that big house all by yourself.

00:51:41.370 --> 00:51:43.895
Now, who would be after you?

00:51:43.937 --> 00:51:47.457
Sophie. Now
that would be a plot twist.

00:51:47.499 --> 00:51:49.693
Candace, shut up. Hope: Sophie.

00:51:49.936 --> 00:51:51.311
We don't use that language.

00:51:51.427 --> 00:51:54.571
Well her parents died and she's
acting like it's a murder mystery game.

00:51:54.613 --> 00:51:56.177
I'm not!

00:51:56.219 --> 00:51:58.339
I'm going to do
lay down. I don't feel well.

00:52:05.200 --> 00:52:08.051
Hey, it's okay.
You're not bothering me.

00:52:08.333 --> 00:52:11.566
I think Sophie's just having a
hard time so don't take it personally.

00:52:13.440 --> 00:52:17.271
You do need to chill out
though. And apologize.

00:52:17.391 --> 00:52:19.391
I will.

00:52:19.680 --> 00:52:21.680
I don't want her
in the room with Sophie.

00:52:22.347 --> 00:52:24.071
Why? Cause of the sleepwalking?

00:52:24.473 --> 00:52:25.692
No, just...

00:52:26.103 --> 00:52:29.196
She's 23. Sophie's not even 17.

00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:31.669
Well, she is kind of her sister.

00:52:32.521 --> 00:52:33.741
Barely.

00:52:34.157 --> 00:52:36.391
They never even lived under the same roof.

00:52:36.747 --> 00:52:40.415
She's a sweet girl and all but we
don't know what kind of influence she is.

00:52:40.962 --> 00:52:43.169
Yeah. Yeah. Good point.

00:52:43.211 --> 00:52:45.000
Alright. I'll offer her the couch.

00:52:45.087 --> 00:52:47.087
Candace can come stay with us.

00:52:47.798 --> 00:52:49.173
She can have her room.

00:52:49.697 --> 00:52:52.598
Uh, no. Candace can
share a room with her sister.

00:52:52.640 --> 00:52:54.640
I can bring the other bed up.

00:52:55.023 --> 00:52:57.023
I want Candace in here with us.

00:52:57.638 --> 00:53:00.615
Why? You don't trust her with Sophie?

00:53:01.474 --> 00:53:04.632
We leave them alone together
all the time. What's changed?

00:53:05.464 --> 00:53:07.464
Sophie has.

00:53:08.365 --> 00:53:10.365
The sleepwalking. The passing out.

00:53:12.080 --> 00:53:15.506
Look, she's - she's just going
through something right now.

00:53:15.548 --> 00:53:17.548
Because of what happened
to John and Melissa.

00:53:18.670 --> 00:53:20.512
Maybe the baby.

00:53:20.554 --> 00:53:21.809
Or...

00:53:21.851 --> 00:53:23.851
Everything else she's been through in life.

00:53:24.998 --> 00:53:26.998
But - that's all it is.

00:53:31.680 --> 00:53:33.714
I hope you're right, Jeremiah Tatum.

00:53:35.353 --> 00:53:37.353
Usually am.

00:53:45.688 --> 00:53:48.568
You know,
your sister is pretty great.

00:53:50.075 --> 00:53:51.606
She's a troublemaker, but...

00:53:52.767 --> 00:53:54.298
Yeah, she's cool.

00:53:54.737 --> 00:53:58.107
That's probably what you would have
been like if my parents got you any sooner.

00:54:00.095 --> 00:54:02.053
I wasn't an easy kid.

00:54:02.095 --> 00:54:06.349
No, you were fine. I mean, you had some
trouble in school, but like that's typical.

00:54:06.817 --> 00:54:09.417
But, I mean - I guess
that's all they really cared about.

00:54:09.604 --> 00:54:13.212
They didn't give a crap about what
I did as long as I got good grades and-

00:54:13.254 --> 00:54:14.551
Kept myself busy.

00:54:14.850 --> 00:54:16.137
But you...

00:54:16.684 --> 00:54:19.960
They didn't know what to do with you.
But that's their fault. That's not yours.

00:54:24.490 --> 00:54:25.878
Um.

00:54:27.074 --> 00:54:31.261
A couple days before they
told me about your birth-mother.

00:54:32.589 --> 00:54:33.646
Yeah?

00:54:33.688 --> 00:54:36.449
I tried to convince them
not to say anything to your parents.

00:54:36.491 --> 00:54:38.335
But um... did they?

00:54:38.635 --> 00:54:40.198
No.

00:54:40.240 --> 00:54:41.356
I told them.

00:54:41.877 --> 00:54:43.211
Really?

00:54:43.253 --> 00:54:45.956
Yeah. I wasn't sure how they'd react.

00:54:46.727 --> 00:54:49.586
I was scared. Really scared.

00:54:50.699 --> 00:54:52.055
But, um...

00:54:52.445 --> 00:54:55.657
They always say that the word
divorce isn't in their vocabulary.

00:54:56.052 --> 00:54:58.052
With each other or us kids, so...

00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:02.063
Everything is fine.

00:55:03.089 --> 00:55:05.751
Good. Good, I'm glad. Um.

00:55:05.793 --> 00:55:07.140
And you're not like...

00:55:07.182 --> 00:55:09.182
You're not like - having
any symptoms, right?

00:55:10.107 --> 00:55:12.059
I haven't plucked anyone's eyes out.

00:55:12.101 --> 00:55:15.000
And
I'm not hearing voices, so...

00:55:15.715 --> 00:55:17.012
Good.

00:55:57.040 --> 00:55:59.592
"You will keep her
perfect peace whose mind

00:55:59.634 --> 00:56:02.286
is stayed on you
because she trusts in You."

00:56:06.815 --> 00:56:09.243
"You'll keep her in
perfect peace whose mind

00:56:09.285 --> 00:56:11.754
is stayed on you
because she trusts in you."

00:56:21.360 --> 00:56:24.635
Make it stop. Make it stop. Make it stop.

00:56:24.677 --> 00:56:27.849
Make it stop. Make it stop. Make
it stop. Sophie. Sophie!

00:56:41.920 --> 00:56:43.539
I'm so sorry.

00:56:44.796 --> 00:56:46.796
What's wrong with you?

00:56:47.894 --> 00:56:49.269
You didn't hear that?

00:57:08.240 --> 00:57:10.055
Dear God.

00:57:10.201 --> 00:57:14.153
Please help Sophie with
whatever she's hearing.

00:57:14.661 --> 00:57:16.661
Help her to...

00:57:17.396 --> 00:57:19.029
Help her feel better.

00:57:19.382 --> 00:57:21.542
Get some sleep.

00:57:23.200 --> 00:57:25.644
You know what's
bothering her. Please fix it.

00:57:30.720 --> 00:57:32.547
It's going to be okay.

00:57:51.766 --> 00:57:52.979
They'll be okay.

00:57:57.040 --> 00:57:59.545
I'll wait up to make sure. You go relax.

00:58:00.807 --> 00:58:02.807
How can I relax?

00:58:04.219 --> 00:58:05.829
Do you trust me?

00:58:13.290 --> 00:58:15.000
I'll be in soon.

00:59:34.170 --> 00:59:35.530
Candy?

00:59:39.200 --> 00:59:40.320
Look what she did to me.

00:59:45.520 --> 00:59:47.322
Wake up. Wake up. Wake up.

00:59:47.634 --> 00:59:50.103
Wake up. Wake up. Wake up. Wake up.

01:01:21.920 --> 01:01:22.901
Good morning, honey.

01:01:22.943 --> 01:01:24.240
Morning.

01:01:25.200 --> 01:01:27.825
How'd you sleep last
night after we woke you up?

01:01:28.175 --> 01:01:30.000
Good. For the most part.

01:01:30.859 --> 01:01:32.625
I prayed for you, too.

01:01:32.737 --> 01:01:34.268
Thank you, honey.

01:01:36.560 --> 01:01:37.668
Are you okay?

01:01:37.980 --> 01:01:38.874
Mhm.

01:01:46.240 --> 01:01:47.444
What is that?

01:01:47.649 --> 01:01:48.712
What?

01:01:50.262 --> 01:01:51.169
Ow.

01:01:51.239 --> 01:01:52.364
Ow.

01:01:52.754 --> 01:01:54.113
It's a bruise?

01:01:54.539 --> 01:01:55.489
I guess.

01:01:56.582 --> 01:02:00.000
I fell last night when
Sophie had the nightmare.

01:02:00.906 --> 01:02:03.202
Or whatever it was.

01:02:06.487 --> 01:02:07.924
You fell?

01:02:08.862 --> 01:02:10.251
Or she pushed you?

01:02:10.433 --> 01:02:12.121
I fell, Mom.

01:02:23.293 --> 01:02:25.596
"I've heard many such things.

01:02:26.064 --> 01:02:27.877
Miserable comforters are you all."

01:02:28.775 --> 01:02:31.165
Dang. Tell them, Job.

01:02:31.939 --> 01:02:34.438
They're being
kinda awful. What's their deal?

01:02:35.245 --> 01:02:37.203
Could be lots of things.

01:02:37.245 --> 01:02:38.805
I think sometimes, people...

01:02:38.952 --> 01:02:40.609
Don't know what to say and they

01:02:40.613 --> 01:02:42.432
should probably just
keep their mouths shut.

01:02:43.419 --> 01:02:45.335
Could be self-righteousness.

01:02:46.169 --> 01:02:47.466
Hm.

01:02:54.160 --> 01:02:55.486
I um...

01:02:55.528 --> 01:02:57.245
Didn't know you knew how to cook.

01:02:57.557 --> 01:03:00.312
I know the basics. I
can - I can figure it out.

01:03:01.562 --> 01:03:02.860
Alright.

01:03:04.108 --> 01:03:05.638
Um.

01:03:05.680 --> 01:03:07.351
I saw Candace's arm.

01:03:08.055 --> 01:03:10.346
Was that from, um, Sophie last night?

01:03:11.283 --> 01:03:12.828
Yeah. Um.

01:03:13.972 --> 01:03:15.972
She... said she fell.

01:03:16.733 --> 01:03:18.533
Yeah, she told me the same thing.

01:03:19.158 --> 01:03:22.969
Um, but you know what? Whatever
happened, Sophie isn't violent.

01:03:23.360 --> 01:03:26.014
And sleepwalking
can be dangerous for anyone.

01:03:26.716 --> 01:03:29.084
But just... don't worry
about that. You know.

01:03:29.126 --> 01:03:32.864
The last thing we need is you stressed.
We don't want the baby stressed. So, just

01:03:32.906 --> 01:03:34.084
like relax. Okay?

01:03:37.520 --> 01:03:38.764
I'll try.

01:03:47.120 --> 01:03:47.991
Come in.

01:03:50.880 --> 01:03:51.914
Miss Ingraham.

01:03:52.233 --> 01:03:54.702
Hi. Uh. You wanted to talk
to me about the Castellis?

01:03:54.832 --> 01:03:55.817
Yes, I...

01:03:56.604 --> 01:04:00.385
It might not be relevant but
when I heard that it wasn't an accident

01:04:00.427 --> 01:04:02.003
I felt like I should tell you.

01:04:02.045 --> 01:04:03.251
Um.

01:04:03.293 --> 01:04:07.011
I went for a walk and I passed Melissa's

01:04:07.053 --> 01:04:10.645
and I saw Sophie waiting at the door.

01:04:11.504 --> 01:04:15.000
Maybe about 45 minutes later

01:04:15.390 --> 01:04:18.610
I was headed back home
and I could hear them arguing.

01:04:18.652 --> 01:04:22.412
It sounded pretty heated,
but

01:04:22.454 --> 01:04:24.103
you know, people argue.

01:04:24.145 --> 01:04:25.956
I didn't think much of it.

01:04:26.424 --> 01:04:28.694
And then I heard something break.

01:04:29.675 --> 01:04:30.894
Break?

01:04:32.080 --> 01:04:34.400
Sounded like something got knocked over.

01:04:34.442 --> 01:04:36.384
I waited and

01:04:36.426 --> 01:04:38.854
I saw Sophie leave and...

01:04:40.259 --> 01:04:42.925
Melissa came to the door afterwards.

01:04:42.967 --> 01:04:46.861
No one looked hurt, so I
decided to mind my own business.

01:04:49.048 --> 01:04:51.066
Okay, thanks for letting me know.

01:04:52.863 --> 01:04:56.071
Please feel free to call me directly if
you think of or remember anything else.

01:04:56.810 --> 01:05:00.000
I will. I hope you find who did this.

01:05:00.508 --> 01:05:01.571
Whatever happened.

01:05:02.110 --> 01:05:04.110
I'm sure we will.

01:05:15.760 --> 01:05:17.880
That
sacrifice that brought us in,

01:05:17.922 --> 01:05:22.088
that's a sacrifice
that only a parent can understand.

01:05:22.400 --> 01:05:23.717
Think about it.

01:05:23.759 --> 01:05:30.000
God and Jesus
together in harmony forever, for eternity.

01:05:30.896 --> 01:05:36.594
Sinless Jesus, perfect
Jesus, and God gives Him up.

01:05:36.636 --> 01:05:41.651
He gives Him up so
we could be saved and more than that,

01:05:41.693 --> 01:05:45.000
adopted into his family.

01:05:45.743 --> 01:05:48.067
I know
we're adoption focused

01:05:48.109 --> 01:05:50.575
in this church. I know
we're all about adoption.

01:05:50.617 --> 01:05:54.509
This is different. Mothers,
look at me. I'm talking to you.

01:05:54.576 --> 01:05:56.656
Hear me
now, cause you'll get this.

01:05:57.008 --> 01:06:02.137
Remember what it was like to
carry your child in your womb.

01:06:02.179 --> 01:06:08.392
Remember what it was like. The joy you felt
when you saw them take their first steps.

01:06:08.434 --> 01:06:13.735
Remember what it was like when
you heard those first words in your ears.

01:06:14.665 --> 01:06:16.665
Now, imagine

01:06:17.241 --> 01:06:20.878
giving your child up. The one you carried.

01:06:20.920 --> 01:06:24.381
To
endure the most horrible,

01:06:24.423 --> 01:06:28.752
bloodied, brutal battering unto death.

01:06:29.688 --> 01:06:32.817
All for the delinquent,

01:06:32.859 --> 01:06:36.924
disrespectful, disobedient
child down the street.

01:08:46.240 --> 01:08:48.111
I didn't want to do it.

01:08:48.153 --> 01:08:50.475
I didn't have any choice. I'm sorry.

01:09:25.760 --> 01:09:27.109
Candie?

01:09:48.240 --> 01:09:49.484
Mommy.

01:09:53.701 --> 01:09:55.933
I - is that you?

01:10:07.442 --> 01:10:08.620
Mommy.

01:10:10.644 --> 01:10:12.525
I know
we all love our children,

01:10:12.567 --> 01:10:14.215
mothers. We love our biological children.

01:10:14.257 --> 01:10:16.502
We love
the ones we carried.

01:10:16.544 --> 01:10:20.187
But this
death, this brutal beating

01:10:20.229 --> 01:10:25.688
was for the one who
caused the death to be necessary.

01:10:25.730 --> 01:10:29.959
It is this undeserved
deliverance that brings us adoption.

01:10:30.001 --> 01:10:34.266
It is the one
who deserves the penalty

01:10:35.076 --> 01:10:37.251
but we give up our best

01:10:37.293 --> 01:10:40.820
to bring them
into our home and adopt them.

01:10:40.862 --> 01:10:43.643
This is our hope.

01:11:26.968 --> 01:11:29.600
Hey. Hey. What's up?

01:11:29.642 --> 01:11:31.981
We're going to
have to question Sophie.

01:11:32.295 --> 01:11:35.700
Of course she's a minor
so you can be there with her.

01:11:36.667 --> 01:11:40.776
Okay. I can bring her in
the morning before work.

01:11:41.088 --> 01:11:42.998
Has there been a development?

01:11:43.040 --> 01:11:44.783
Unfortunately.

01:11:44.825 --> 01:11:47.573
Could be nothing, but
we do have some questions.

01:11:48.024 --> 01:11:49.712
Alright, see you tomorrow.

01:12:10.844 --> 01:12:11.829
Hm.

01:12:14.000 --> 01:12:16.655
Did you have another
nightmare? Hm? No.

01:12:17.398 --> 01:12:18.461
Just, uh.

01:12:18.736 --> 01:12:21.517
Just going to go to the
bathroom and get a snack.

01:12:22.513 --> 01:12:26.701
Snack? Is that what you call
an entire gallon of ice cream?

01:12:27.164 --> 01:12:29.164
Land whale.

01:12:42.008 --> 01:12:43.396
Well, help yourself.

01:12:44.411 --> 01:12:47.440
Oh, I am so sorry.

01:12:50.720 --> 01:12:54.114
I promise to buy you guys a new gallon.
I didn't even eat that much. I swear.

01:12:55.461 --> 01:12:57.461
Don't worry about it.

01:12:58.800 --> 01:13:00.000
You okay?

01:13:00.315 --> 01:13:02.398
Yeah. Um.

01:13:02.440 --> 01:13:05.048
Just like stressed about everything.

01:13:05.090 --> 01:13:08.767
Ice cream therapy always helps,
ya know? Um, how about you?

01:13:08.809 --> 01:13:10.163
Mm.

01:13:10.475 --> 01:13:13.259
Same. And I don't even like ice cream.

01:13:13.301 --> 01:13:16.925
Maybe the baby does. Mm. Maybe.

01:13:17.315 --> 01:13:20.623
Um, you do get to rest
during the day, I hope?

01:13:20.961 --> 01:13:23.586
Yeah. A little bit too much.

01:13:26.480 --> 01:13:29.454
You know, I worked through
my entire first pregnancy.

01:13:29.496 --> 01:13:32.835
That was like 10 years ago. Hm.

01:13:33.381 --> 01:13:35.606
Still, I shouldn't be this slow.

01:13:35.648 --> 01:13:38.142
No, every pregnancy is different.

01:13:38.184 --> 01:13:40.584
And you and your family have
been through so much this year.

01:13:44.720 --> 01:13:46.640
That might be part of
what keeps me up at night.

01:13:49.600 --> 01:13:53.987
I quit my job to be a stay at
home mom to Candace and the

01:13:54.029 --> 01:13:57.088
two or three other kids I was
just sure we were going to have.

01:13:57.412 --> 01:13:59.605
But it...

01:13:59.647 --> 01:14:04.958
ended up being two
miscarriages and a lot of infertility.

01:14:06.285 --> 01:14:08.838
I'm so sorry, Hope. That's terrible.

01:14:09.371 --> 01:14:12.621
Never got this far along. They were early.

01:14:13.524 --> 01:14:16.143
But, you know, sometimes it does

01:14:17.581 --> 01:14:20.206
make me think that I just

01:14:21.688 --> 01:14:23.513
Don't want to mess this one up.

01:14:23.555 --> 01:14:26.467
You didn't mess anything
up with the others.

01:14:26.509 --> 01:14:28.549
You know, sometimes
those things just happen.

01:14:28.591 --> 01:14:30.358
But you can't dwell on that right now.

01:14:31.215 --> 01:14:32.825
Yeah, I know.

01:14:35.200 --> 01:14:36.481
I -

01:14:36.523 --> 01:14:40.714
I should be consoling you after your
parents, not the other way around.

01:14:40.756 --> 01:14:44.503
No. No. No. You and your baby
are the most important things right now.

01:14:45.000 --> 01:14:47.078
And honestly, just being here,

01:14:47.120 --> 01:14:49.512
seeing a happy
family has been so helpful.

01:14:49.554 --> 01:14:54.098
I'm not letting it remind
me of how cold things were at home.

01:14:54.140 --> 01:14:56.170
I'm just doing my best to

01:14:56.212 --> 01:14:58.663
enjoy the moment, like be in the present.

01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:01.375
I'll try that.

01:15:06.880 --> 01:15:08.261
Mom! Mommy!

01:15:12.088 --> 01:15:14.268
Candie? Are you okay?

01:15:14.310 --> 01:15:16.775
Is the baby okay? What's
wrong with the baby?

01:15:16.866 --> 01:15:20.091
No. Nothing. Nothing.
Baby, why? What happened?

01:15:20.133 --> 01:15:23.158
I knocked over the trash can
and there was blood and I was

01:15:23.200 --> 01:15:25.108
scared that something happened.

01:15:26.513 --> 01:15:28.094
Okay.

01:15:28.719 --> 01:15:31.287
All right. Just Just wait here. Okay?

01:15:52.985 --> 01:15:54.438
The hell?

01:15:57.600 --> 01:15:59.301
Oh, um, I can explain.

01:16:08.880 --> 01:16:11.937
I don't know. I think the
door opening might have woke me up.

01:16:11.979 --> 01:16:15.000
Or I could just tell that I
wasn't alone in the room.

01:16:19.560 --> 01:16:21.560
Make it stop.

01:16:23.920 --> 01:16:25.585
Make it stop.

01:16:26.437 --> 01:16:28.437
Sophie. Are you okay?

01:16:28.919 --> 01:16:30.919
Make it stop.

01:16:31.520 --> 01:16:32.840
Make it stop.

01:16:33.699 --> 01:16:37.192
Make it stop.

01:16:37.800 --> 01:16:39.800
Make it stop.

01:16:40.112 --> 01:16:42.070
Make it stop.

01:16:42.112 --> 01:16:44.112
Make it stop.

01:16:44.888 --> 01:16:46.888
Make it stop.

01:16:50.000 --> 01:16:51.575
Make it stop.

01:16:52.903 --> 01:16:55.733
Make it stop. Make it stop.

01:16:56.774 --> 01:16:58.774
Make it stop.

01:16:59.120 --> 01:17:02.511
Make it stop. Make it stop.

01:17:03.058 --> 01:17:08.371
Make it stop. Make it stop. Make it stop.

01:17:08.413 --> 01:17:14.118
Make it stop. Make
it stop. Make it stop. Make it stop.

01:17:14.160 --> 01:17:17.666
Make it stop. Make it stop.
Make it stop. Make it stop. Make it stop.

01:17:17.917 --> 01:17:20.383
Make it stop. Make it
stop. Make it stop. Make it stop.

01:17:20.387 --> 01:17:23.204
Make it stop.
Make it stop. Make it stop.

01:17:23.246 --> 01:17:25.246
Make it stop. Make it stop. Make it stop.

01:17:25.945 --> 01:17:28.701
Ow! Sophie, relax. It's just me.

01:17:31.200 --> 01:17:34.425
What happened? What happened to your arm?

01:17:42.000 --> 01:17:44.958
How did I even get in here? I'm
so sorry. I don't It's fine.

01:17:45.000 --> 01:17:46.739
It's okay. Hey, it's okay. Just um

01:17:47.047 --> 01:17:49.672
Hand me the knife. Please?

01:17:58.640 --> 01:18:01.756
Um, let's just go back to bed.

01:18:04.880 --> 01:18:06.843
I woke Candace up
and moved her back to her bed.

01:18:06.847 --> 01:18:09.813
Ah, and then I went to check on
Sophie but she was already asleep.

01:18:10.360 --> 01:18:12.942
I mean, I don't - I don't even
think she'd remember any of it.

01:18:12.984 --> 01:18:14.684
Maybe she thought she was dreaming.

01:18:16.402 --> 01:18:20.448
Well, you should get to the hospital...
in case you - you need stitches.

01:18:20.490 --> 01:18:23.653
No, I didn't want to leave
in the middle of the night. And I -

01:18:23.695 --> 01:18:25.410
wouldn't know what to tell them.

01:18:25.688 --> 01:18:27.298
What do you mean?

01:18:28.197 --> 01:18:30.571
I can't say that Sophie
stabbed me in her sleep.

01:18:30.613 --> 01:18:32.462
Not with the investigation going on.

01:18:32.907 --> 01:18:34.427
I mean, what - what would they think?

01:18:38.320 --> 01:18:41.817
So, do we talk to Sophie
now or let her sleep?

01:18:42.910 --> 01:18:46.236
Like you she needs to rest. So, I
think we should talk in the morning.

01:18:48.735 --> 01:18:50.406
Okay.

01:18:50.797 --> 01:18:52.781
I - I am so sorry, Brooke.

01:18:53.333 --> 01:18:56.114
No, it - it's fine. I just, I
just hope Sophie's okay.

01:18:57.779 --> 01:19:00.657
Alright. Well, you get to the hospital and

01:19:00.699 --> 01:19:02.699
we'll call you. Okay.

01:19:09.680 --> 01:19:12.720
They were threatening to tell
your parents about Sheila's condition?

01:19:12.968 --> 01:19:13.937
Yes.

01:19:15.000 --> 01:19:17.073
And were you planning to hide it from them?

01:19:17.561 --> 01:19:18.702
No.

01:19:19.407 --> 01:19:22.500
Then... what was the argument about?

01:19:23.008 --> 01:19:24.657
I just didn't... uh -

01:19:25.180 --> 01:19:28.664
Look I - I just wanted to
tell them in my own time.

01:19:31.920 --> 01:19:34.493
Were you having possible
symptoms of schizophrenia?

01:19:37.930 --> 01:19:39.425
Then why hide it?

01:19:41.065 --> 01:19:43.976
Because I'm 16.

01:19:44.288 --> 01:19:46.406
What if it happens in two years?

01:19:47.032 --> 01:19:49.098
What if it happens in two months? I -

01:19:49.140 --> 01:19:52.442
What if it never happens and
I brought it up for no reason?

01:19:52.832 --> 01:19:54.960
It's a lot to find out.

01:19:55.002 --> 01:19:56.455
Okay?

01:19:57.394 --> 01:20:00.000
I was going to talk to my
parents when I was ready.

01:20:00.410 --> 01:20:02.566
But - but they were pushing me.

01:20:03.172 --> 01:20:05.013
And that made you angry?

01:20:05.055 --> 01:20:06.555
Obviously, yes.

01:20:06.597 --> 01:20:11.167
They weren't worried about the Tatums. They
were just trying to cover their own asses.

01:20:11.209 --> 01:20:13.875
And they didn't care how it affected me.

01:20:15.066 --> 01:20:17.300
Have you had any symptoms since then?

01:20:18.460 --> 01:20:19.757
Is that relevant?

01:20:20.426 --> 01:20:21.880
Maybe.

01:20:44.800 --> 01:20:47.162
Someone claimed Sophie
had violent sleepwalking

01:20:47.204 --> 01:20:49.257
episodes that caused all these injuries.

01:20:50.586 --> 01:20:52.705
What does this have
to do with the Castellis?

01:20:55.360 --> 01:20:57.297
It's my job. I got to ask.

01:21:01.280 --> 01:21:03.269
Where were you the night they died, Sophie?

01:21:06.080 --> 01:21:07.146
I was home.

01:21:08.708 --> 01:21:12.340
Are you sure? There's no
chance you had another episode?

01:21:16.720 --> 01:21:18.656
Do we have to do this?

01:21:19.906 --> 01:21:23.263
She said she was home, Kayla.
Do you have any other questions?

01:21:25.840 --> 01:21:29.238
No, not right now. But...
if you remember anything,

01:21:29.280 --> 01:21:32.387
like anything at all, Sophie,
you need to let us know, okay?

01:21:41.680 --> 01:21:44.646
Hi, Candace.

01:21:44.688 --> 01:21:45.837
Hi.

01:21:45.879 --> 01:21:49.413
Candace. This is Brittany
Etters. She would like to talk to you.

01:21:50.279 --> 01:21:51.558
Hi.

01:21:51.600 --> 01:21:53.777
Candace. It is so great to meet you.

01:21:53.819 --> 01:21:57.815
Your principal has had many
wonderful things to say about you.

01:21:58.752 --> 01:22:00.580
Thank you.

01:22:00.970 --> 01:22:02.333
Uh.

01:22:02.375 --> 01:22:04.375
Do you work for the district?

01:22:04.538 --> 01:22:07.788
I'm with D-C-P and P.

01:22:09.576 --> 01:22:12.564
Division of Child Protective serv...

01:22:12.606 --> 01:22:15.384
Protection and permanency.

01:22:16.321 --> 01:22:18.798
Shouldn't one of my parents be here?

01:22:19.345 --> 01:22:21.032
Have a seat.

01:22:30.560 --> 01:22:33.760
Legally, we don't need
a parent present to talk.

01:22:36.240 --> 01:22:37.766
What is this about?

01:22:39.094 --> 01:22:45.000
Could you show me the
back of your left arm, please?

01:22:58.000 --> 01:22:59.181
If I don't?

01:23:01.680 --> 01:23:03.198
I'll assume

01:23:03.667 --> 01:23:05.674
that you have something to hide

01:23:07.236 --> 01:23:09.415
and this case will be escalated.

01:23:21.280 --> 01:23:22.561
I fell.

01:23:23.264 --> 01:23:26.663
Who was in the room with
you when you fell, Candace?

01:23:34.160 --> 01:23:36.326
Whose room were you in?

01:23:37.029 --> 01:23:39.213
My sister.

01:23:39.255 --> 01:23:42.110
She didn't mean to hurt
me. It was an accident.

01:24:44.480 --> 01:24:46.043
What are we going to do?

01:24:47.371 --> 01:24:49.133
I don't know.

01:24:51.866 --> 01:24:54.257
And what is wrong with me, Jer?

01:24:55.719 --> 01:24:57.261
I haven't

01:24:57.303 --> 01:24:59.294
been able to stay out of bed. I.

01:25:00.312 --> 01:25:03.434
It took everything in me to not

01:25:03.476 --> 01:25:07.356
just break down in front that
guidance counselor and cry

01:25:07.398 --> 01:25:10.541
like some little beotch or something.

01:25:12.571 --> 01:25:16.112
This isn't me. That's not
me. Not even under pressure.

01:25:16.236 --> 01:25:18.236
Especially not under pressure.

01:25:20.720 --> 01:25:22.550
But you are pregnant.

01:25:22.940 --> 01:25:27.253
It's not the pregnancy. It
wasn't like this the first time.

01:25:27.295 --> 01:25:29.448
Well, each pregnancy is different.

01:25:29.490 --> 01:25:32.432
And we're dealing
with a lot more than we were before.

01:25:33.814 --> 01:25:35.424
And

01:25:36.243 --> 01:25:37.696
you're old, now.

01:25:40.320 --> 01:25:41.829
You're not funny.

01:25:47.608 --> 01:25:49.762
What do we do about Sophie?

01:25:51.089 --> 01:25:54.825
Do we get her evaluated?

01:25:57.680 --> 01:25:59.647
You really think she has schizophrenia?

01:25:59.689 --> 01:26:01.652
I don't know. But...

01:26:10.320 --> 01:26:13.118
I don't feel safe.

01:26:13.743 --> 01:26:16.326
Not for Candace.
Not - not for the baby.

01:26:16.478 --> 01:26:18.478
We have to do something.

01:26:19.430 --> 01:26:21.126
Hope.

01:26:21.168 --> 01:26:25.188
And I know. I know I'm probably
wrong, but I can't help how I feel.

01:26:25.230 --> 01:26:29.091
And I feel like something bad is
going to happen. Something that...

01:26:29.133 --> 01:26:31.316
that we can't reverse.

01:26:42.640 --> 01:26:44.686
She wasn't home that night, Jer.

01:26:50.344 --> 01:26:51.875
What night?

01:26:55.840 --> 01:26:57.897
The night John and Melissa died.

01:27:59.760 --> 01:28:03.191
They're going to
leave you like everyone else has.

01:28:04.987 --> 01:28:08.097
You are
always going to be alone, Sophie.

01:28:08.139 --> 01:28:10.021
Always. Forever.

01:28:10.063 --> 01:28:11.529
Kill them.

01:28:11.571 --> 01:28:14.497
Stop. Stop. Rip her stomach open.

01:28:14.539 --> 01:28:16.302
Now. Stop!

01:28:16.344 --> 01:28:19.648
Remember who they
were before they turned on you.

01:28:19.722 --> 01:28:21.689
Kill them, now.

01:28:21.731 --> 01:28:23.690
Before it's too late.

01:28:23.732 --> 01:28:24.876
Before it's too late.

01:28:24.880 --> 01:28:27.056
Kill them. Kill yourself.

01:28:27.098 --> 01:28:29.478
You're
always going to be alone.

01:28:29.520 --> 01:28:33.768
You'll always be
alone, Sophie.

01:28:48.488 --> 01:28:50.440
Stop!

01:28:52.080 --> 01:28:53.291
Jer?

01:28:54.307 --> 01:28:55.916
Jer, did you hear that?

01:29:05.600 --> 01:29:08.084
I'm sorry, but I have to make it stop.

01:29:11.130 --> 01:29:12.444
What?

01:29:12.486 --> 01:29:14.609
The voices.

01:29:14.651 --> 01:29:16.644
They're coming from inside you.

01:29:23.360 --> 01:29:24.719
Sophie.

01:29:25.188 --> 01:29:28.598
It started right around the
time you got pregnant, Hope.

01:29:28.640 --> 01:29:30.195
Don't you realize that?

01:29:30.237 --> 01:29:32.238
The voices,

01:29:32.280 --> 01:29:34.713
the knocking, the blackouts, everything.

01:29:36.508 --> 01:29:38.960
That's not a baby in there, Hope.

01:29:39.002 --> 01:29:42.328
He knows how long
you've wanted another kid.

01:29:42.640 --> 01:29:45.868
How many times you've
begged God to let you get pregnant again.

01:29:46.493 --> 01:29:49.747
God didn't listen. But he did.

01:29:52.480 --> 01:29:53.869
Sophie.

01:29:53.911 --> 01:29:55.785
Put the knife down.

01:29:56.097 --> 01:29:58.906
If it's born, it's going to kill you.

01:29:59.389 --> 01:30:02.379
I have to cut out right
now before it's too late.

01:30:02.848 --> 01:30:07.054
Sophie, please, I don't want to hurt you.

01:30:08.480 --> 01:30:13.032
This is for you, Hope. I'm
protecting you. All of you.

01:30:22.560 --> 01:30:25.075
Wake up. Wake up. Wake up.

01:30:26.403 --> 01:30:29.485
Wake up. It's
not a dream this time, Hope.

01:30:31.137 --> 01:30:34.057
Wake up. Wake up. Wake up.

01:30:35.228 --> 01:30:39.390
Wake up. Wake up. Wake up. Wake up.

01:30:39.432 --> 01:30:41.078
Wake up! Wake up!

01:30:41.120 --> 01:30:43.901
Hope. Hope. Look at me.

01:30:44.317 --> 01:30:46.317
Look at me.

01:30:48.960 --> 01:30:53.669
I can't do it anymore. I can't
do it. I can't take these dreams.

01:30:59.760 --> 01:31:01.224
You guys okay?

01:31:01.266 --> 01:31:04.737
Yeah, it's
just a dream. She's fine.

01:31:07.040 --> 01:31:10.137
Do you know where Sophie
is? She's not in her room.

01:31:12.011 --> 01:31:14.141
Come stay with your mom.

01:31:24.266 --> 01:31:25.641
Damn it.

01:31:27.360 --> 01:31:28.566
Sophie!

01:31:32.080 --> 01:31:35.087
She's not in
the house. I'll be back.

01:31:35.477 --> 01:31:37.009
We should call Kayla.

01:31:38.274 --> 01:31:40.274
What if she comes back and she's...

01:31:41.461 --> 01:31:44.208
We can't just let her go. You
lock the door if you need to.

01:31:45.000 --> 01:31:46.125
I know.

01:31:46.594 --> 01:31:47.719
Find her.

01:32:33.600 --> 01:32:36.749
Dear God, please
help Daddy find Sophie.

01:32:37.062 --> 01:32:39.883
I want her to
know that I love her very much.

01:32:40.196 --> 01:32:42.860
And I miss her. And...

01:32:45.280 --> 01:32:47.779
I don't know, we kind of just

01:32:48.248 --> 01:32:52.812
got distanced since
this whole thing started.

01:32:54.160 --> 01:32:58.844
I miss her and I really want
her to know that I'm there for her.

01:33:00.000 --> 01:33:03.001
And please help mommy
with her nightmares and

01:33:04.189 --> 01:33:05.529
Let them stop.

01:33:06.466 --> 01:33:11.025
Can you please fix whatever
is happening with our family right now?

01:33:22.800 --> 01:33:24.884
You remember this place?

01:33:25.587 --> 01:33:27.257
You were sitting right there.

01:33:28.975 --> 01:33:30.787
First time Candace and I saw you.

01:33:33.520 --> 01:33:36.240
Candace wanted to get on the
swing next to me and asked if I'd mind.

01:33:39.120 --> 01:33:41.859
I told her you'd look like
you wanted to be left alone.

01:33:42.952 --> 01:33:45.000
She said maybe you needed a friend.

01:33:48.880 --> 01:33:50.543
How'd you know I'd be here?

01:33:53.120 --> 01:33:55.377
It's the last thing you looked up on maps.

01:33:59.360 --> 01:34:01.078
You forgot the way?

01:34:01.390 --> 01:34:02.999
Yep.

01:34:03.624 --> 01:34:06.142
There's another way I know
there's something wrong with me.

01:34:08.720 --> 01:34:10.007
I'm sorry, but

01:34:10.866 --> 01:34:12.655
I don't want to hurt you guys.

01:34:13.905 --> 01:34:18.033
And after everything that's been
taken away from me my whole life

01:34:19.516 --> 01:34:20.983
I can't -

01:34:21.686 --> 01:34:23.663
I can't live without you, too.

01:34:24.912 --> 01:34:26.880
You wouldn't have to.

01:34:28.676 --> 01:34:30.572
I see how Hope looks at me.

01:34:31.509 --> 01:34:33.584
She's scared.

01:34:34.443 --> 01:34:36.467
And she should be.

01:34:38.810 --> 01:34:41.887
Hope is stressed

01:34:42.980 --> 01:34:45.000
and she's worried, but

01:34:45.498 --> 01:34:47.566
she loves you like all of us do.

01:34:48.034 --> 01:34:51.075
And we're all going to get through this.

01:34:51.700 --> 01:34:53.394
Whatever it is.

01:34:55.112 --> 01:34:57.505
Even if I killed John and Melissa?

01:35:03.440 --> 01:35:04.705
I don't think I did.

01:35:05.720 --> 01:35:07.219
I don't think I could.

01:35:12.400 --> 01:35:14.253
Did you go to their house that night?

01:35:18.080 --> 01:35:19.376
Yes.

01:35:19.418 --> 01:35:22.306
Yes, I wanted to steal the
folder even though I knew

01:35:23.087 --> 01:35:25.346
it wouldn't fix anything.

01:35:26.830 --> 01:35:28.883
And then I blacked out.

01:35:29.430 --> 01:35:32.143
I - I don't know what happened.

01:35:40.480 --> 01:35:42.712
Sophie, when we adopted you

01:35:45.680 --> 01:35:47.739
We chose you

01:35:47.781 --> 01:35:50.204
and we chose everything
that comes with you.

01:35:50.907 --> 01:35:53.781
I don't think
you have schizophrenia.

01:35:54.328 --> 01:35:56.617
I don't think
you could hurt anyone.

01:35:58.257 --> 01:36:03.606
But even if you did, we would
still choose you all over again.

01:36:08.160 --> 01:36:09.531
If I go back

01:36:10.702 --> 01:36:13.389
and I hurt Candace

01:36:14.092 --> 01:36:15.780
or the baby

01:36:16.873 --> 01:36:19.383
would you be able to live with that?

01:36:23.600 --> 01:36:24.970
No.

01:36:33.680 --> 01:36:35.107
But if I went home without you,

01:36:37.840 --> 01:36:39.585
I couldn't live with that either.

01:36:40.834 --> 01:36:42.557
None of us could.

01:36:49.040 --> 01:36:51.105
And you won't give up on me?

01:36:53.448 --> 01:36:55.067
Never.

01:37:36.670 --> 01:37:41.288
Sophie. Don't you ever scare me
like that again. Do you hear me?

01:37:42.069 --> 01:37:43.606
I'm sorry, Mom.

01:38:22.640 --> 01:38:24.355
Is Sophie home?

01:38:24.667 --> 01:38:26.518
Yeah.

01:38:28.080 --> 01:38:30.234
She's out there with your dad.

01:38:31.405 --> 01:38:33.304
Is she going to stay?

01:38:37.600 --> 01:38:39.722
She's your sister.

01:38:40.269 --> 01:38:43.596
And she always will be.
Nothing is going to change that.

01:38:45.120 --> 01:38:46.730
Promise?

01:38:48.880 --> 01:38:50.863
I promise.

01:39:00.000 --> 01:39:03.787
Are you sure you'll hear me if I get up?

01:39:08.160 --> 01:39:10.016
That's what the bell's for.

01:39:10.719 --> 01:39:14.339
That's if I don't
take it off in my sleep.

01:39:18.640 --> 01:39:21.208
Maybe you should be
behind a locked door, too.

01:39:24.800 --> 01:39:26.044
Sophie.

01:39:27.840 --> 01:39:29.594
Don't say things like that.

01:39:35.920 --> 01:39:38.196
You touch that bell though,

01:39:38.508 --> 01:39:41.395
I'm waking up swinging.

01:39:41.437 --> 01:39:42.582
Just so you know.

01:39:47.520 --> 01:39:48.995
I love you.

01:39:49.542 --> 01:39:50.941
I love you, too.

01:40:09.680 --> 01:40:11.074
Hey.

01:40:12.011 --> 01:40:14.615
I'm going to take Sophie to the doctor.

01:40:14.657 --> 01:40:17.158
I can do that, honey.
You already took off yesterday.

01:40:18.329 --> 01:40:21.103
As of this morning, I don't
go back till next Wednesday.

01:40:22.040 --> 01:40:25.223
I thought it'd be good for all of us
to get out of town for a few days.

01:40:25.535 --> 01:40:26.989
Maybe go to Lancaster.

01:40:28.317 --> 01:40:30.151
We can afford all that?

01:40:30.193 --> 01:40:32.528
I can pick up extra
shifts when we get back.

01:40:34.245 --> 01:40:36.745
And I think the fresh air
would be good for all of us.

01:40:37.839 --> 01:40:39.523
Fresh air?

01:40:40.617 --> 01:40:43.387
Smells like horse piss
out there.

01:40:47.760 --> 01:40:49.324
That aside,

01:40:51.120 --> 01:40:52.878
I do think that'd be good.

01:40:55.768 --> 01:40:56.968
Good.

01:41:18.080 --> 01:41:19.180
You okay?

01:41:19.571 --> 01:41:20.900
Yeah.

01:41:24.648 --> 01:41:26.556
You need anything?

01:41:26.598 --> 01:41:27.606
No.

01:41:28.622 --> 01:41:31.577
All right. I think I'm going
to go lie down for a bit.

01:41:32.160 --> 01:41:35.830
Okay. Wait Mom, do you want to... Um...

01:41:35.872 --> 01:41:39.958
Take a walk or go get some
exercise and kick a ball around?

01:41:40.000 --> 01:41:43.762
It helps when you're not feeling
well to get some exercise and sunlight.

01:41:45.312 --> 01:41:47.565
And where did you learn that from?

01:41:47.955 --> 01:41:51.185
Sophie and I looked up some
pregnancy stuff. We think you're

01:41:51.227 --> 01:41:55.343
prenatally depressed.
It happens to 10 to 20% of women.

01:41:56.198 --> 01:41:58.198
Prenatally depressed?

01:41:59.362 --> 01:42:01.158
Anyways

01:42:01.200 --> 01:42:04.863
You can either pop pills or
get some exercise and sunlight.

01:42:04.905 --> 01:42:06.690
Or both. Your choice.

01:42:08.720 --> 01:42:10.920
Third option. Nap.

01:42:10.962 --> 01:42:13.038
No. Come on.

01:42:14.311 --> 01:42:16.623
Come on. Get up.

01:42:22.800 --> 01:42:26.270
Look, a
psychiatric exam wouldn't hurt. Um.

01:42:26.312 --> 01:42:30.000
There's a practice that I
could, uh, recommend on the third floor.

01:42:30.625 --> 01:42:33.878
But other than that, everything that you've
described seems to be consistent with

01:42:33.920 --> 01:42:35.737
post-concussive syndrome.

01:42:35.779 --> 01:42:38.023
You know, the thumping

01:42:38.065 --> 01:42:40.362
that you hear, that could
be a form of tinnitus.

01:42:42.080 --> 01:42:44.669
Isn't that usually more
like a ringing in the ears?

01:42:44.711 --> 01:42:47.238
Yeah, usually. Um but every now and then

01:42:47.280 --> 01:42:49.733
the brain interprets that information as a

01:42:49.775 --> 01:42:52.518
like a percussive type of
thing. You could hear knocking.

01:42:52.560 --> 01:42:55.281
You could hear thumping.
Sometimes you could even hear buzzing.

01:42:55.285 --> 01:42:56.175
Um

01:42:57.581 --> 01:42:59.010
Have you gotten sick?

01:42:59.052 --> 01:43:01.244
Uh, any nausea? Vomiting?

01:43:01.634 --> 01:43:05.486
Yeah, I was puking every day
for like a week after my first

01:43:05.528 --> 01:43:07.608
um, blackout.

01:43:08.501 --> 01:43:10.111
Hm.

01:43:11.208 --> 01:43:12.739
Well...

01:43:13.412 --> 01:43:17.088
For now all I'm going to recommend is rest.

01:43:17.130 --> 01:43:20.239
Make sure you get some
good rest. Uh, also melatonin.

01:43:20.281 --> 01:43:24.766
For sleep and, um,
I'm also going to recommend an MRI.

01:43:26.327 --> 01:43:28.033
There's an imaging place

01:43:28.075 --> 01:43:32.379
just downstairs that also might be
able to take you today if you hurry.

01:43:34.800 --> 01:43:36.638
Uh, what would an MRI be looking for?

01:43:37.086 --> 01:43:40.579
Brain bleed. Uh, you know, fracture.

01:43:40.621 --> 01:43:42.420
Like I'm pretty sure

01:43:42.462 --> 01:43:46.502
You're fine. I'm
98% there, but I want to be 100%.

01:43:46.544 --> 01:43:47.838
Is that okay?

01:43:51.440 --> 01:43:52.877
Okay.

01:43:52.919 --> 01:43:54.901
All right, guys. I'll be right back.

01:44:05.600 --> 01:44:08.160
So, everything started that night
after you went to their house?

01:44:08.931 --> 01:44:10.072
Yeah.

01:44:10.619 --> 01:44:12.460
I was just standing there

01:44:13.163 --> 01:44:15.321
and then I woke up.

01:44:16.267 --> 01:44:18.033
With a concussion.

01:44:39.920 --> 01:44:42.169
Stop!
Remember who they were

01:44:42.211 --> 01:44:44.198
before they turned on you.

01:44:44.240 --> 01:44:45.959
Kill them now.

01:44:46.001 --> 01:44:49.001
Before it's too
late. Before it's too late.

01:44:49.043 --> 01:44:51.627
Kill them. Kill yourself.

01:44:51.669 --> 01:44:54.138
You're
always going to be alone.

01:44:55.680 --> 01:44:58.962
What's the matter? I
heard something last night.

01:44:59.799 --> 01:45:01.799
Don't know what it was.

01:45:02.320 --> 01:45:05.537
I guess I couldn't
remember up until now

01:45:05.849 --> 01:45:08.798
because I was so tired.

01:45:09.760 --> 01:45:13.939
But when Sophie was screaming,
I definitely heard something.

01:46:07.040 --> 01:46:08.898
There might be more in the house.

01:46:08.940 --> 01:46:11.680
Maybe we should go outside.
If Sophie's the target, then

01:46:12.070 --> 01:46:14.859
I doubt they would have
put things anywhere else. But

01:46:14.901 --> 01:46:16.730
yeah, we should check.

01:46:18.480 --> 01:46:22.944
There's only been one other
person in this house recently

01:46:22.986 --> 01:46:24.693
besides Kayla.

01:46:30.160 --> 01:46:33.238
So I called the investigator from
the insurance company and of course

01:46:33.280 --> 01:46:37.318
they looked into Brooke right away. She
stood to gain the most from their deaths,

01:46:37.360 --> 01:46:39.771
but she was in New
York the night they died.

01:46:39.813 --> 01:46:42.971
And it's likely the
tampering was done that day.

01:46:43.440 --> 01:46:45.362
They're certain she was in New York?

01:46:45.404 --> 01:46:48.617
Yes. Security camera confirmed her story

01:46:48.659 --> 01:46:50.709
that she was in two different stores.

01:46:51.256 --> 01:46:54.317
One was 7-Eleven around 11:00 p.m.

01:46:54.708 --> 01:46:56.858
She said she's got the munchies.

01:46:58.029 --> 01:47:01.607
Right. So she just so
happened to be seen on camera

01:47:01.649 --> 01:47:03.945
at the exact time that she needed to be.

01:47:04.335 --> 01:47:06.339
Yeah, it's a little convenient.

01:47:06.381 --> 01:47:09.895
She couldn't have been working
with somebody? Giving them information?

01:47:12.160 --> 01:47:13.763
I'll see what I can find out.

01:47:14.622 --> 01:47:16.598
Are you sure you don't
want me to take the...

01:47:16.640 --> 01:47:17.952
No. I-

01:47:17.994 --> 01:47:20.760
I think if we touch it,
they'll know we're on to them.

01:47:35.520 --> 01:47:37.882
You want me to take a shift? No.

01:47:41.840 --> 01:47:45.000
Keep staring like that. You're going
to strain your eyes, start seeing things.

01:47:46.423 --> 01:47:48.930
I'll let you know when I get tired.

01:47:49.320 --> 01:47:51.676
Which will probably be never.

01:47:52.066 --> 01:47:54.817
Do you have any idea how exciting this is?

01:47:55.208 --> 01:47:56.960
Oh yeah. Riveting.

01:47:57.819 --> 01:48:01.857
I don't know what I want
to do with my life yet, but

01:48:01.899 --> 01:48:04.619
this is making a good
case for law enforcement.

01:48:07.064 --> 01:48:09.627
Sophie this is like 3% of the job.

01:48:10.017 --> 01:48:12.530
Maybe four if you're a detective.

01:48:12.657 --> 01:48:13.893
Now,

01:48:13.935 --> 01:48:17.025
become a private investigator,
you practically live in your car.

01:48:17.337 --> 01:48:18.767
And you don't get shot at.

01:48:20.017 --> 01:48:21.957
So why are you doing security, then?

01:48:22.582 --> 01:48:26.227
Cuz you don't always have a partner to
relieve you when you want to take a nap.

01:48:27.710 --> 01:48:30.028
Let's start our own business, then.

01:48:30.070 --> 01:48:32.774
What? I'm serious.

01:48:33.242 --> 01:48:36.207
That way we can get you away
from that school before it gets

01:48:36.597 --> 01:48:38.008
shot up or something.

01:48:39.023 --> 01:48:41.300
Now why would you say something like that?

01:48:41.342 --> 01:48:43.358
It could happen.

01:48:46.170 --> 01:48:48.086
I know.

01:48:49.023 --> 01:48:51.297
And God forbid, but

01:48:51.339 --> 01:48:55.264
if it did, I think I'd have a
pretty good shot at stopping it.

01:48:56.436 --> 01:48:58.586
Yeah. Well, you know what?

01:48:58.628 --> 01:49:00.625
I think we'd all rather
you not have to do that.

01:49:02.026 --> 01:49:06.186
Even though it is pretty
awesome that you'd be willing to.

01:49:12.902 --> 01:49:15.000
Eyes on the environment, rookie.

01:49:21.773 --> 01:49:24.320
Dad. Hm?

01:49:56.000 --> 01:49:59.445
He has a key but he
comes through the woods.

01:50:00.000 --> 01:50:02.187
Either he doesn't drive

01:50:02.229 --> 01:50:05.412
or they have a vehicle they don't
want associated with the house.

01:50:06.028 --> 01:50:07.803
Should we go see where he parked?

01:50:09.131 --> 01:50:10.437
Yeah.

01:50:11.139 --> 01:50:13.253
Yeah, I don't want to
start the van up, though.

01:50:13.643 --> 01:50:15.332
We can take the woods like he did.

01:50:15.956 --> 01:50:17.129
Okay.

01:50:17.755 --> 01:50:21.051
Just wait 3 minutes. Just to be sure.

01:50:28.080 --> 01:50:30.590
This will be easier on our eyes

01:50:30.632 --> 01:50:33.095
and harder for anyone
else to see from a distance.

01:50:33.486 --> 01:50:35.059
You learn that as a cop?

01:50:35.372 --> 01:50:39.065
No your sneaky investigative
journalist of a mom taught me that.

01:50:40.627 --> 01:50:42.410
All right, let's go.

01:51:12.240 --> 01:51:15.230
Alright, go get a picture of
the license plate for Kayla.

01:51:15.777 --> 01:51:18.750
Then we can get home. Kay.

01:52:45.280 --> 01:52:48.403
The car belongs to Dexter
Ambrose. He's from New York

01:52:48.445 --> 01:52:51.139
a couple of towns over
from where Brooke went to college.

01:52:51.181 --> 01:52:55.408
No known association, but it's
at least of note that he's down here now.

01:52:55.450 --> 01:52:57.063
Yeah, I would say so.

01:52:57.105 --> 01:53:00.366
He's a bad guy. Convicted
felon.

01:53:00.408 --> 01:53:03.784
Armed robbery, aggravated
assault with a deadly weapon.

01:53:03.826 --> 01:53:07.089
Possession of a deadly
weapon, assault on a police officer.

01:53:07.401 --> 01:53:09.739
And this is who Brooke
is spending her time with.

01:53:10.208 --> 01:53:12.251
We're still going through footage.

01:53:12.293 --> 01:53:16.547
One doorbell camera recorded a car
that looked very similar to his passing by

01:53:16.589 --> 01:53:20.000
twice, maybe 200 yards from
where Jeremiah and Sophie saw it.

01:53:20.547 --> 01:53:22.491
On the night of the murders.

01:53:22.533 --> 01:53:24.226
Are you going to
be able to question him?

01:53:24.230 --> 01:53:25.777
Have to find him first.

01:53:26.480 --> 01:53:28.949
Brooke was too smart
to deny knowing him, but

01:53:28.991 --> 01:53:32.131
she said she doesn't know
where he is or where he's staying.

01:53:32.600 --> 01:53:35.240
We'll close
in. It'll just take time.

01:53:35.282 --> 01:53:38.239
If I get any major updates,
I'll let you know. Otherwise,

01:53:38.281 --> 01:53:39.611
you guys enjoy the quiet.

01:53:39.845 --> 01:53:43.672
Give her a nice stress-free
couple days out there. Okay, Jeremiah?

01:53:43.714 --> 01:53:45.373
You got it.

01:53:45.685 --> 01:53:47.609
Bye, guys. Love you both.

01:53:48.078 --> 01:53:49.590
Love you, too.

01:54:06.960 --> 01:54:11.080
Yeah, that's hers. She wears them to
bed at night. I've seen that exact one.

01:54:11.549 --> 01:54:14.424
Why the hell is
her headband near my car?

01:54:15.000 --> 01:54:19.313
You've been made. They were probably
watching at some point. Maybe overnight.

01:54:19.440 --> 01:54:20.878
She must have dropped it.

01:54:22.128 --> 01:54:24.191
So, you think she knows?

01:54:24.233 --> 01:54:26.360
Knows what? What you're up to?

01:54:27.141 --> 01:54:28.760
Nothing they can prove.

01:54:29.229 --> 01:54:31.073
What if they looked up my car?

01:54:31.115 --> 01:54:32.629
So, what if they did?

01:54:34.659 --> 01:54:37.274
You said the police are
asking questions again.

01:54:37.665 --> 01:54:41.050
Your aunt and uncle don't
buy the changes to the will. If -

01:54:41.092 --> 01:54:43.636
If these people start asking
questions again-I didn't cut the wire.

01:54:43.640 --> 01:54:45.312
So I have nothing to worry about.

01:54:46.060 --> 01:54:47.699
The hell is that supposed to mean?

01:54:47.741 --> 01:54:49.623
Would you just calm down?

01:54:49.665 --> 01:54:52.408
Jeez, how did you last a
day in prison being such a...?

01:54:52.798 --> 01:54:54.158
Watch it.

01:54:55.095 --> 01:54:57.143
I'm not going back to prison for you.

01:54:57.185 --> 01:54:59.958
And you won't. Okay, just relax.

01:55:00.000 --> 01:55:01.810
Trust me, they don't have anything.

01:55:02.279 --> 01:55:03.420
What if they do?

01:55:04.435 --> 01:55:07.166
Then we'll just give them
more reason to suspect Sophie.

01:55:11.851 --> 01:55:13.157
I'm listening.

01:55:13.199 --> 01:55:16.528
Okay, so they're away somewhere.

01:55:16.570 --> 01:55:18.541
If we can figure out where

01:55:18.583 --> 01:55:21.184
we can make it look like a murder suicide

01:55:21.226 --> 01:55:24.583
and then that'll give them more reason
to suspect that Sophie killed my parents.

01:55:24.625 --> 01:55:28.899
And if she knows anything about
you, then she'd no longer be a witness.

01:55:36.240 --> 01:55:41.124
Did you see this earlier? We should come
back after the baby's born. It's perfect.

01:55:41.166 --> 01:55:43.130
I'm down.

01:55:43.520 --> 01:55:45.802
Sleep in, okay? We have
a hard day tomorrow.

01:55:46.349 --> 01:55:49.787
More farms, more ice
cream. We need the rest.

01:55:54.160 --> 01:55:57.800
Can you not stand there? I hate doing this.

01:55:58.737 --> 01:56:02.317
Candace, your mom's just doing
what any good parent would do.

01:56:03.567 --> 01:56:05.861
You would never hurt me.

01:56:05.903 --> 01:56:07.789
Brooke's a liar.

01:56:07.831 --> 01:56:09.486
Maybe.

01:56:09.876 --> 01:56:11.390
But we have to be sure.

01:56:11.702 --> 01:56:13.380
Night, Sophie.

01:56:15.928 --> 01:56:17.090
Good night.

01:58:43.120 --> 01:58:46.331
What are you doing with that? She's
supposed to shoot everyone, isn't she?

01:58:46.335 --> 01:58:48.969
No. The kid needs to be a mess.

01:58:49.011 --> 01:58:51.798
It needs to look like she
snapped and then killed her parents

01:58:51.840 --> 01:58:52.909
out of remorse.

01:58:54.705 --> 01:58:58.422
Look, I'll do everything
else, but the kid's yours then.

01:58:59.970 --> 01:59:01.267
Whatever.

01:59:05.920 --> 01:59:07.310
All right, let's go.

01:59:07.857 --> 01:59:09.795
Before she gets up we
need to get Sophie situated

01:59:09.837 --> 01:59:11.857
and then we need to figure
out where the guns are.

02:00:05.600 --> 02:00:07.436
Don't move.

02:00:07.478 --> 02:00:09.615
Don't even look at me.

02:00:10.240 --> 02:00:11.735
Drop the knife.

02:00:28.720 --> 02:00:30.360
I'm going to kill you.

02:00:34.890 --> 02:00:37.918
Why'd you bring a knife
instead of another gun?

02:00:39.168 --> 02:00:41.951
You got that from the
kitchen here, didn't you?

02:00:46.720 --> 02:00:48.334
Were you going to frame me again?

02:00:49.505 --> 02:00:51.667
Is that the idea?

02:01:04.240 --> 02:01:07.918
Who were you going to use this on? Hm. Me?

02:01:07.960 --> 02:01:09.316
Or Candace?

02:01:09.941 --> 02:01:12.121
How do you know she isn't already dead?

02:01:12.746 --> 02:01:14.602
Her door is locked

02:01:15.000 --> 02:01:16.857
and I was listening.

02:01:16.899 --> 02:01:19.845
I wouldn't have let you
anywhere near her. Trust me.

02:01:21.408 --> 02:01:23.665
You planned this?

02:01:29.600 --> 02:01:31.703
You were the one making plans, Brooke.

02:01:33.030 --> 02:01:34.722
Frame me,

02:01:34.764 --> 02:01:36.743
kill John and Melissa,

02:01:37.055 --> 02:01:38.795
kill my family.

02:01:39.497 --> 02:01:40.586
Right?

02:01:45.600 --> 02:01:48.296
But you and your friend are
the only ones dying today.

02:01:48.765 --> 02:01:51.042
You don't have to kill me. No?

02:01:54.400 --> 02:01:58.261
Your parents can die. My family
can die. But you get to live?

02:02:02.400 --> 02:02:04.205
Get on your knees.

02:02:05.142 --> 02:02:06.685
Sophie.

02:02:07.154 --> 02:02:08.682
Now.

02:02:26.800 --> 02:02:28.881
You know what I did to protect my mom?

02:02:28.923 --> 02:02:30.374
Hope.

02:02:32.248 --> 02:02:36.160
You want to know what I would do to someone
who was going to stab my little sister?

02:02:37.440 --> 02:02:39.082
And frame me for it?

02:02:44.080 --> 02:02:46.259
Sophie, please.

02:03:03.440 --> 02:03:05.120
Did you see the gun?

02:03:08.488 --> 02:03:09.903
No.

02:03:12.480 --> 02:03:15.000
We should call the cops. Then mom and dad.

02:03:21.280 --> 02:03:23.291
You're not going to kill her.

02:03:24.462 --> 02:03:25.381
Right?

02:03:29.520 --> 02:03:30.853
No.

02:03:33.040 --> 02:03:34.672
Go to your room.

02:03:34.714 --> 02:03:37.205
I'm going to go outside
and check how they got in.

02:03:37.247 --> 02:03:38.831
Then I'll be right there.

02:03:46.320 --> 02:03:49.057
I won't hurt her. I promise.

02:04:09.120 --> 02:04:11.343
Um, uh, I'm doing a lot better now.

02:04:11.890 --> 02:04:16.175
You taking anything? No.
No, that is a last resort.

02:04:16.217 --> 02:04:18.109
I am just

02:04:18.151 --> 02:04:23.240
going for walks and getting
exercise, going outside

02:04:24.021 --> 02:04:28.072
Talking through my feelings
like I am now, I guess.

02:04:28.114 --> 02:04:30.164
I even joined a virtual support group.

02:04:30.206 --> 02:04:32.867
Good. Got to take care of yourself.

02:04:34.273 --> 02:04:37.153
The baby seems healthy
even after everything.

02:04:37.195 --> 02:04:41.611
Yeah. Yeah, the baby's fine. Um,

02:04:42.080 --> 02:04:45.348
everything looked good this morning.
So, we're actually going to go out.

02:04:45.390 --> 02:04:47.662
Have a picnic when Jeremiah gets home.

02:04:47.704 --> 02:04:49.115
It's supposed to be nice out.

02:04:49.157 --> 02:04:52.261
Where is my invite?

02:04:52.303 --> 02:04:54.131
You're more than welcome.

02:04:54.173 --> 02:04:57.319
I've got to get in early
tomorrow to do some paperwork,

02:04:57.361 --> 02:05:00.456
but maybe I'll be able to get out in time.

02:05:06.000 --> 02:05:07.360
Did you um

02:05:07.402 --> 02:05:11.258
ever figure out how Brooke and her
friend knew where we were staying?

02:05:11.949 --> 02:05:14.225
Um. That's not important.

02:05:14.537 --> 02:05:15.957
Kayla.

02:05:17.049 --> 02:05:19.118
You and the baby don't
need any more stress.

02:05:19.160 --> 02:05:20.792
I'm not going to stress about it.

02:05:21.183 --> 02:05:23.486
Really. What's done is done.

02:05:23.876 --> 02:05:25.297
Come on. Out with it.

02:05:25.922 --> 02:05:28.571
Sophie posted some pictures on her

02:05:29.040 --> 02:05:30.967
"gram thing". I don't know.

02:05:31.009 --> 02:05:34.943
It was a story which means it
goes away after certain amount of time.

02:05:37.520 --> 02:05:40.274
I am more familiar with social
media than you are. Clearly.

02:05:40.899 --> 02:05:42.832
Whatever.

02:05:43.145 --> 02:05:45.907
She posted pictures of your vacation and

02:05:45.949 --> 02:05:48.282
Brooke saw them and she figured it out.

02:05:48.751 --> 02:05:50.877
It's not Sophie's fault, though.

02:05:51.360 --> 02:05:53.868
You know how the
kids are and she didn't post

02:05:53.910 --> 02:05:56.189
the address or anything like that.

02:05:56.970 --> 02:05:58.806
Just, please don't say anything to her.

02:05:58.848 --> 02:06:00.138
I won't.

02:06:00.685 --> 02:06:02.509
She's a good kid.

02:06:04.071 --> 02:06:05.225
Yeah.

02:06:05.850 --> 02:06:07.289
She is.

02:06:08.772 --> 02:06:10.435
Coffee?

02:06:10.904 --> 02:06:12.337
Sure.

02:06:35.053 --> 02:06:37.208
What the hell
is she doing in there?

02:06:37.598 --> 02:06:39.809
She must have just woke up.

02:06:40.121 --> 02:06:42.371
I didn't feel her that much this morning.

02:06:43.386 --> 02:06:45.982
Eh. You sure it's not just gas?

02:06:46.024 --> 02:06:48.528
You are all bloated and gross and

02:06:48.570 --> 02:06:52.379
Okay. I'm going to smack you. Let me
finish. I was going to say "and beautiful".

02:06:57.377 --> 02:06:59.424
We should play tag!

02:07:00.000 --> 02:07:02.659
We're way too old to
be playing tag, Candace.

02:07:03.440 --> 02:07:07.716
You're so boring. Let's
just take a nice nap, Candy.

02:07:12.480 --> 02:07:14.486
You're it. Ow.

02:07:18.000 --> 02:07:22.691
You know, I've been
thinking. We went 10 years.

02:07:23.628 --> 02:07:26.237
Even after IVF and

02:07:26.862 --> 02:07:29.674
everything else that we
tried.

02:07:30.767 --> 02:07:32.473
And then we adopt Sophie.

02:07:33.254 --> 02:07:36.152
And not even a year later, here we are.

02:07:39.120 --> 02:07:42.016
Yeah. I think we would have
adopted her even if we had another kid.

02:07:42.058 --> 02:07:43.627
Maybe.

02:07:44.063 --> 02:07:46.185
But who knows where
our lives would have been?

02:07:47.981 --> 02:07:51.800
Maybe she wouldn't have wanted
to babysit two or three kids.

02:07:53.440 --> 02:07:55.410
Maybe you guys would
have been too distracted

02:07:55.452 --> 02:07:57.895
to notice her at the park that day.

02:08:00.160 --> 02:08:02.032
Yeah, I don't like to think about that.

02:08:05.520 --> 02:08:07.274
I'm just thinking

02:08:10.320 --> 02:08:12.555
even though it was hard

02:08:13.336 --> 02:08:15.312
because we have her now.

02:08:15.641 --> 02:08:17.633
Everything was worth it.

02:08:28.800 --> 02:08:32.690
Did Kayla ever mention how Brooke
found out where we were staying?

02:08:34.252 --> 02:08:35.699
Yeah.

02:08:39.760 --> 02:08:41.992
I didn't say anything, but

02:08:43.007 --> 02:08:46.718
I mean, Sophie doesn't really
post that much on social media.

02:08:48.253 --> 02:08:50.521
Don't you think it's a little odd

02:08:50.563 --> 02:08:53.095
that she chose to that day?

02:09:05.760 --> 02:09:07.256
No.

02:09:07.298 --> 02:09:09.006
Not really.

02:09:10.880 --> 02:09:12.196
You?

02:09:23.285 --> 02:09:24.884
No.

02:09:25.353 --> 02:09:27.745
I guess not.

02:10:18.240 --> 02:10:22.960
CAPTIONS PROVIDED BY SHADY DAWN PICTURES
